{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XkwAPvRBTWmnepJ5FcVRRh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。 使用已生成的 counterfactual pairs (n=100)，每个 judge 做 dual-direction pairwise， position control。与 GPT-4o baseline (69.1%, p=0.006) 对比。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"gpt4o_formal_win_rate\": 0.691,\n7\t      \"gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.006,\n8\t      \"gpt4o_n_consistent\": 55,\n9\t      \"gpt4o_formal_wins\": 38,\n10\t      \"gpt4o_casual_wins\": 17,\n11\t      \"claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate\": 0.64,\n12\t      \"claude_sonnet_sign_test_p\": 0.028,\n13\t      \"claude_sonnet_n_consistent\": 50,\n14\t      \"claude_sonnet_formal_wins\": 32,\n15\t      \"claude_sonnet_casual_wins\": 18,\n16\t      \"claude_sonnet_consistency_rate\": 0.51,\n17\t      \"gemini_flash_formal_win_rate\": 0.724,\n18\t      \"gemini_flash_sign_test_p\": 0.002,\n19\t      \"gemini_flash_n_consistent\": 58,\n20\t      \"gemini_flash_formal_wins\": 42,\n21\t      \"gemini_flash_casual_wins\": 16,\n22\t      \"gemini_flash_consistency_rate\": 0.59,\n23\t      \"n_judges_significant_after_holm\": 3,\n24\t      \"holm_corrected_p_values\": {\n25\t        \"gemini\": 0.006,\n26\t        \"gpt4o\": 0.012,\n27\t        \"claude\": 0.028\n28\t      },\n29\t      \"cross_judge_mean_winrate\": 0.685,\n30\t      \"cross_judge_winrate_range\": [\n31\t        0.64,\n32\t        0.724\n33\t      ],\n34\t      \"cross_judge_pairwise_p_median\": 0.006\n35\t    },\n36\t    \"tables\": [\n37\t      {\n38\t        \"title\": \"Table 2: Formality Pairwise Results Across Judges (LLMBar, n=100)\",\n39\t        \"columns\": [\n40\t          \"Judge\",\n41\t          \"n_consistent\",\n42\t          \"Formal Wins\",\n43\t          \"Casual Wins\",\n44\t          \"Win Rate\",\n45\t          \"95% CI\",\n46\t          \"Sign Test p\",\n47\t          \"Holm p\"\n48\t        ],\n49\t        \"rows\": [\n50\t          [\n51\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n52\t            55,\n53\t            38,\n54\t            17,\n55\t            \"69.1%\",\n56\t            \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\",\n57\t            \"0.006**\",\n58\t            \"0.012*\"\n59\t          ],\n60\t          [\n61\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n62\t            50,\n63\t            32,\n64\t            18,\n65\t            \"64.0%\",\n66\t            \"[50.1%, 75.9%]\",\n67\t            \"0.028*\",\n68\t            \"0.028*\"\n69\t          ],\n70\t          [\n71\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n72\t            58,\n73\t            42,\n74\t            16,\n75\t            \"72.4%\",\n76\t            \"[59.8%, 82.3%]\",\n77\t            \"0.002**\",\n78\t            \"0.006**\"\n79\t          ]\n80\t        ]\n81\t      }\n82\t    ],\n83\t    \"figures\": [],\n84\t    \"analysis\": \"A1 假设成立：3/3 judge 在 Holm correction 后显著。cross_judge_mean_winrate 0.685 在 [0.60, 0.75] 范围中上。Judge 间量级差异 (Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定， 为 C3 axis-dependency 提供 judge 维度证据。Direction asymmetry 在所有 judge 上存在 (formal-original 方向更强)，为 exp-005 original preference 控制提供动机。\\n\\n\\nFormality bias 是 LLM judge 的通用现象而非 GPT-4o 特有。三个 judge 的 RLHF 训练数据 普遍偏向 formal/professional 风格回答，formal text 与 higher-quality content 在 pretraining 语料中高度相关。Claude-Sonnet 效应略弱 (0.64) 因为 Anthropic 的 RLHF 有更多 helpfulness 导向校准，对 surface style 依赖稍低；Gemini-Flash 效应略强 (0.72) 因为轻量模型更依赖 surface heuristics 作为 quality proxy。三者量级差异 (0.64-0.72) 本身也是 C3 evidence—— bias magnitude 是 judge-dependent 的。Holm correction 后全部 p<0.05，因为每个 judge 的 raw p 都足够小 (最大 0.028)，3 重比较惩罚不足以翻转。\\n\"\n85\t  },\n86\t  {\n87\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n88\t    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD 流程。新 counterfactual generation (不同 source text)。 三个 judge (GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash) 分别评测。每个 benchmark n=100。 与 LLMBar 结果交叉比较，形成 3×3 矩阵。\\n\",\n89\t    \"results\": {\n90\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate\": 0.67,\n91\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_p\": 0.012,\n92\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate\": 0.61,\n93\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_p\": 0.048,\n94\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate\": 0.7,\n95\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_p\": 0.004,\n96\t      \"alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass\": 0.9,\n97\t      \"alpacaeval_nli_mean\": 0.908,\n98\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate\": 0.65,\n99\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_p\": 0.018,\n100\t      \"mtbench_claude_formal_winrate\": 0.6,\n101\t      \"mtbench_claude_p\": 0.065,\n102\t      \"mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate\": 0.68,\n103\t      \"mtbench_gemini_p\": 0.008,\n104\t      \"mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass\": 0.87,\n105\t      \"mtbench_nli_mean\": 0.882,\n106\t      \"n_benchmarks_with_gap\": 3,\n107\t      \"significant_combos_total\": 7,\n108\t      \"total_combos\": 9,\n109\t      \"non_significant_combos\": [\n110\t        \"Claude×MT-Bench (p=0.065, borderline)\"\n111\t      ],\n112\t      \"borderline_combos\": 1,\n113\t      \"mean_winrate_across_all_9\": 0.664\n114\t    },\n115\t    \"tables\": [\n116\t      {\n117\t        \"title\": \"Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)\",\n118\t        \"columns\": [\n119\t          \"Judge\",\n120\t          \"LLMBar\",\n121\t          \"AlpacaEval\",\n122\t          \"MT-Bench\",\n123\t          \"Mean\"\n124\t        ],\n125\t        \"rows\": [\n126\t          [\n127\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n128\t            \"69.1%**\",\n129\t            \"67.0%*\",\n130\t            \"65.0%*\",\n131\t            \"67.0%\"\n132\t          ],\n133\t          [\n134\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n135\t            \"64.0%*\",\n136\t            \"61.0%*\",\n137\t            \"60.0%†\",\n138\t            \"61.7%\"\n139\t          ],\n140\t          [\n141\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n142\t            \"72.4%**\",\n143\t            \"70.0%**\",\n144\t            \"68.0%**\",\n145\t            \"70.1%\"\n146\t          ],\n147\t          [\n148\t            \"Mean\",\n149\t            \"68.5%\",\n150\t            \"66.0%\",\n151\t            \"64.3%\",\n152\t            \"66.3%\"\n153\t          ]\n154\t        ],\n155\t        \"footnote\": \"** p<0.01, * p<0.05, † p<0.10. n=100 per cell, n_consistent varies 48-58.\"\n156\t      },\n157\t      {\n158\t        \"title\": \"Table 4: Counterfactual Quality per Benchmark\",\n159\t        \"columns\": [\n160\t          \"Benchmark\",\n161\t          \"n\",\n162\t          \"NLI Pass Rate\",\n163\t          \"NLI Mean\",\n164\t          \"BERTScore Mean\"\n165\t        ],\n166\t        \"rows\": [\n167\t          [\n168\t            \"LLMBar\",\n169\t            100,\n170\t            \"88%\",\n171\t            0.896,\n172\t            0.842\n173\t          ],\n174\t          [\n175\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n176\t            100,\n177\t            \"90%\",\n178\t            0.908,\n179\t            0.851\n180\t          ],\n181\t          [\n182\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n183\t            100,\n184\t            \"87%\",\n185\t            0.882,\n186\t            0.835\n187\t          ]\n188\t        ]\n189\t      }\n190\t    ],\n191\t    \"figures\": [],\n192\t    \"analysis\": \"A2 假设成立：3/3 benchmarks 显示 gap。Benchmark 梯度 (LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench) 有方法论意义——task-specific evaluation criteria 越强，style bias 越被抑制。 Judge 梯度 (Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定跨 benchmark，说明 judge 的 style sensitivity 是其内在属性而非 benchmark artifact。9 个组合的 mean win rate 0.664 在 cross_judge_formal_win_rate [0.60, 0.75] 范围内。\\n\\n\\nFormality bias 跨 benchmark 泛化，因为 bias 源于 judge 内在偏好而非特定数据集特征。 AlpacaEval 效应略强于 MT-Bench：open-ended instruction-following 任务给 style variation 更大空间，formal tone 作为 quality proxy 权重更大；MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构和更 specific 的评判标准 (如 math/reasoning accuracy) 部分抑制了 style 影响。Claude×MT-Bench 是唯一 borderline 不显著的组合 (p=0.065)，因为 Claude 在有明确正确性标准的 benchmark 上更倾向 content-based 判断，且 Claude 本身 formality sensitivity 最低。NLI pass rate 在 AlpacaEval (0.90) 略高于 MT-Bench (0.87)，因为 AlpacaEval response 结构更简单， counterfactual 改写更容易保持语义。7/9 显著远超偶然水平。\\n\"\n193\t  },\n194\t  {\n195\t    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n196\t    \"description\": \"对 exp-001/002 的每个 judge×benchmark 组合，计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统性比较两种 measurement 的 sensitivity。同一 counterfactual 数据。\\n\",\n197\t    \"results\": {\n198\t      \"llmbar_gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.1,\n199\t      \"llmbar_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.332,\n200\t      \"llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_p\": 0.006,\n201\t      \"llmbar_claude_likert_ate\": 0.06,\n202\t      \"llmbar_claude_likert_p\": 0.485,\n203\t      \"llmbar_claude_pairwise_p\": 0.028,\n204\t      \"llmbar_gemini_likert_ate\": 0.14,\n205\t      \"llmbar_gemini_likert_p\": 0.198,\n206\t      \"llmbar_gemini_pairwise_p\": 0.002,\n207\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.08,\n208\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.412,\n209\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_likert_ate\": 0.04,\n210\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_likert_p\": 0.551,\n211\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_likert_ate\": 0.12,\n212\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_likert_p\": 0.142,\n213\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.09,\n214\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.388,\n215\t      \"mtbench_claude_likert_ate\": 0.03,\n216\t      \"mtbench_claude_likert_p\": 0.612,\n217\t      \"mtbench_gemini_likert_ate\": 0.11,\n218\t      \"mtbench_gemini_likert_p\": 0.175,\n219\t      \"combos_with_gap\": 7,\n220\t      \"combos_without_gap\": 2,\n221\t      \"combos_total\": 9,\n222\t      \"gap_note\": \"2 个无 gap：Claude×MT-Bench (两者都不显著，一致性 non-sig)，Gemini×AlpacaEval Likert p=0.142 borderline\",\n223\t      \"median_likert_p\": 0.388,\n224\t      \"median_pairwise_p\": 0.012,\n225\t      \"cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median\": 0.37,\n226\t      \"no_reverse_pattern\": true\n227\t    },\n228\t    \"tables\": [\n229\t      {\n230\t        \"title\": \"Table 5: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — The Likert Blindspot\",\n231\t        \"columns\": [\n232\t          \"Judge × Benchmark\",\n233\t          \"Likert ATE\",\n234\t          \"Likert p\",\n235\t          \"Pairwise WR\",\n236\t          \"Pairwise p\",\n237\t          \"Gap?\"\n238\t        ],\n239\t        \"rows\": [\n240\t          [\n241\t            \"GPT-4o × LLMBar\",\n242\t            \"+0.10\",\n243\t            \"0.332\",\n244\t            \"69.1%\",\n245\t            \"0.006**\",\n246\t            \"✓\"\n247\t          ],\n248\t          [\n249\t            \"Claude × LLMBar\",\n250\t            \"+0.06\",\n251\t            \"0.485\",\n252\t            \"64.0%\",\n253\t            \"0.028*\",\n254\t            \"✓\"\n255\t          ],\n256\t          [\n257\t            \"Gemini × LLMBar\",\n258\t            \"+0.14\",\n259\t            \"0.198\",\n260\t            \"72.4%\",\n261\t            \"0.002**\",\n262\t            \"✓\"\n263\t          ],\n264\t          [\n265\t            \"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\",\n266\t            \"+0.08\",\n267\t            \"0.412\",\n268\t            \"67.0%\",\n269\t            \"0.012*\",\n270\t            \"✓\"\n271\t          ],\n272\t          [\n273\t            \"Claude × AlpacaEval\",\n274\t            \"+0.04\",\n275\t            \"0.551\",\n276\t            \"61.0%\",\n277\t            \"0.048*\",\n278\t            \"✓\"\n279\t          ],\n280\t          [\n281\t            \"Gemini × AlpacaEval\",\n282\t            \"+0.12\",\n283\t            \"0.142\",\n284\t            \"70.0%\",\n285\t            \"0.004**\",\n286\t            \"✓\"\n287\t          ],\n288\t          [\n289\t            \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\",\n290\t            \"+0.09\",\n291\t            \"0.388\",\n292\t            \"65.0%\",\n293\t            \"0.018*\",\n294\t            \"✓\"\n295\t          ],\n296\t          [\n297\t            \"Claude × MT-Bench\",\n298\t            \"+0.03\",\n299\t            \"0.612\",\n300\t            \"60.0%\",\n301\t            \"0.065†\",\n302\t            \"—\"\n303\t          ],\n304\t          [\n305\t            \"Gemini × MT-Bench\",\n306\t            \"+0.11\",\n307\t            \"0.175\",\n308\t            \"68.0%\",\n309\t            \"0.008**\",\n310\t            \"✓\"\n311\t          ]\n312\t        ],\n313\t        \"footnote\": \"Gap = Likert p>0.10 AND Pairwise p<0.05. 7/9 combos show gap. 0/9 reverse pattern.\"\n314\t      }\n315\t    ],\n316\t    \"figures\": [],\n317\t    \"analysis\": \"C2 的核心 evidence。7/9 组合出现系统性 measurement gap，且无 reverse pattern (没有任何组合 Likert 显著但 Pairwise 不显著)。median Likert p = 0.37 在 [0.15, 0.5] 范围内， median Pairwise p = 0.012 在 [0.001, 0.02] 范围内。gap 不依赖特定 judge 或 benchmark—— 这意味着现有文献中基于 Likert 的 style bias 研究可能系统性低估问题严重程度。 Practical implication: style bias audit 应使用 pairwise comparison 而非 pointwise scoring。\\n\\n\\nLikert-Pairwise gap 的根因是 measurement scale 的信息结构差异。Likert pointwise 评分中， style bias 被三个机制稀释：(1) score anchoring——judge 倾向使用量表中段，微小 style 偏好 不足以跨越 score boundary；(2) absolute calibration noise——不同 item 的 baseline quality 差异远大于 style 引入的差异，between-item variance 淹没 within-item style effect； (3) 离散量表的 resolution limit——1-10 scale 上 0.10 的 ATE 被四舍五入吸收。 Pairwise 直接呈现 A/B 对比，消除 absolute calibration 问题，将 style 差异放大为 forced choice 中的 tie-breaking signal。Gemini 的 Likert p (0.142-0.198) 最接近显著， 因为 Gemini 的 formality premium 最强 (72.4%)，即使 Likert 的稀释也无法完全消除。 但仍未达 p<0.05，确认 Likert blindspot 的系统性。\\n\"\n318\t  },\n319\t  {\n320\t    \"name\": \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) — negative control\",\n321\t    \"description\": \"D014 Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。Epistemic commitment change 与 NLI verification 结构性不兼容。本实验以 pilot 数据 (n=20) 为基础，正式文档化失败模式， 作为 C3 的 axis boundary evidence。不需额外 API 调用。\\n\",\n322\t    \"results\": {\n323\t      \"n_pilot\": 20,\n324\t      \"nli_cf_pass_rate\": 0.65,\n325\t      \"nli_cf_mean\": 0.704,\n326\t      \"bertscore_cf_mean\": 0.92,\n327\t      \"joint_pass_rate\": 0.45,\n328\t      \"by_tone_assertive_both_pass\": 0.385,\n329\t      \"by_tone_hedging_both_pass\": 0.571,\n330\t      \"catastrophic_nli_lt001_count\": 6,\n331\t      \"catastrophic_fraction\": 0.3,\n332\t      \"failure_mode\": \"assertive→hedging 改变 epistemic commitment (confidence markers, modal verbs)，NLI 正确检测为 non-entailment\",\n333\t      \"structural_incompatibility\": true,\n334\t      \"pipeline_stopped_at\": \"content_verification\"\n335\t    },\n336\t    \"tables\": [\n337\t      {\n338\t        \"title\": \"Table A1: Tone Axis Content Verification Failure (n=20 pilot)\",\n339\t        \"columns\": [\n340\t          \"Direction\",\n341\t          \"n\",\n342\t          \"NLI Mean\",\n343\t          \"Both Pass Rate\",\n344\t          \"Catastrophic NLI<0.01\"\n345\t        ],\n346\t        \"rows\": [\n347\t          [\n348\t            \"Assertive→Hedging\",\n349\t            13,\n350\t            \"0.656\",\n351\t            \"38.5%\",\n352\t            \"4/13 (30.8%)\"\n353\t          ],\n354\t          [\n355\t            \"Hedging→Assertive\",\n356\t            7,\n357\t            \"0.793\",\n358\t            \"57.1%\",\n359\t            \"2/7 (28.6%)\"\n360\t          ],\n361\t          [\n362\t            \"Overall\",\n363\t            20,\n364\t            \"0.704\",\n365\t            \"45.0%\",\n366\t            \"6/20 (30.0%)\"\n367\t          ]\n368\t        ]\n369\t      }\n370\t    ],\n371\t    \"figures\": [],\n372\t    \"analysis\": \"Tone 作为 negative control 为 C3 提供 principled method boundary：CSD 适用于 不改变认知承诺的 surface-level style axes (formality ✓)，不适用于改变 epistemic commitment 的 axes (tone ✗)。NLI gate 在此处正确拒绝—— 这不是方法失败，而是正确的质量控制行为。Paper 中定位为 \\\"method boundary\\\" 而非 \\\"negative result\\\"，因为它回答了 \\\"CSD 适用范围\\\" 这个审稿人一定会问的问题。\\n\\n\\nTone 改变 (assertive↔hedging) 不是纯 style 变换——它改变了说话者对命题的认知承诺程度。 \\\"X is the best approach\\\" vs \\\"X might be a reasonable approach\\\" 在 NLI 框架下不构成双向蕴含， 因为前者的 truth conditions 严格强于后者。30% 的样本出现 catastrophic NLI<0.01， 说明这不是 threshold 选择问题而是根本性的语义兼容性问题。Hedging 方向 (assertive→hedging) both_pass 更高 (57.1% vs 38.5%)，因为弱化断言仍蕴含弱化后的命题，但强化断言 (hedging→assertive) 引入了原文未承诺的确定性。这个不对称性本身就是 principled boundary 的证据：NLI gate 不是 arbitrary obstacle，而是正确识别了语义改变。\\n\"\n373\t  },\n374\t  {\n375\t    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n376\t    \"description\": \"Original text vs 同风格 double-rewrite 的 pairwise 比较，量化 original preference confound。 D015: 扩展到所有 judge × LLMBar 组合。同时分析 casual-original subset (main pairwise 中原文为 casual 的子集) 在不同 judge 上的 formal win rate。\\n\",\n377\t    \"results\": {\n378\t      \"gpt4o_n_valid\": 95,\n379\t      \"gpt4o_n_consistent\": 60,\n380\t      \"gpt4o_original_wins\": 32,\n381\t      \"gpt4o_rewrite_wins\": 28,\n382\t      \"gpt4o_original_win_rate\": 0.533,\n383\t      \"gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.362,\n384\t      \"gpt4o_wilson_ci\": [\n385\t        0.408,\n386\t        0.655\n387\t      ],\n388\t      \"claude_n_consistent\": 55,\n389\t      \"claude_original_wins\": 28,\n390\t      \"claude_rewrite_wins\": 27,\n391\t      \"claude_original_win_rate\": 0.509,\n392\t      \"claude_sign_test_p\": 0.92,\n393\t      \"gemini_n_consistent\": 62,\n394\t      \"gemini_original_wins\": 34,\n395\t      \"gemini_rewrite_wins\": 28,\n396\t      \"gemini_original_win_rate\": 0.548,\n397\t      \"gemini_sign_test_p\": 0.28,\n398\t      \"mean_original_win_rate\": 0.53,\n399\t      \"any_judge_original_pref_significant\": false,\n400\t      \"casual_orig_gpt4o_formal_wr\": 0.545,\n401\t      \"casual_orig_gpt4o_p\": 0.832,\n402\t      \"casual_orig_gpt4o_n\": 22,\n403\t      \"casual_orig_claude_formal_wr\": 0.63,\n404\t      \"casual_orig_claude_p\": 0.072,\n405\t      \"casual_orig_claude_n\": 27,\n406\t      \"casual_orig_gemini_formal_wr\": 0.611,\n407\t      \"casual_orig_gemini_p\": 0.096,\n408\t      \"casual_orig_gemini_n\": 36,\n409\t      \"casual_orig_best_judge\": \"Claude\",\n410\t      \"casual_orig_best_judge_wr\": 0.63,\n411\t      \"casual_orig_best_judge_p\": 0.072\n412\t    },\n413\t    \"tables\": [\n414\t      {\n415\t        \"title\": \"Table 6: Original Preference Control Across Judges (LLMBar)\",\n416\t        \"columns\": [\n417\t          \"Judge\",\n418\t          \"n_consistent\",\n419\t          \"Original Wins\",\n420\t          \"Rewrite Wins\",\n421\t          \"Original WR\",\n422\t          \"p\"\n423\t        ],\n424\t        \"rows\": [\n425\t          [\n426\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n427\t            60,\n428\t            32,\n429\t            28,\n430\t            \"53.3%\",\n431\t            \"0.362\"\n432\t          ],\n433\t          [\n434\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n435\t            55,\n436\t            28,\n437\t            27,\n438\t            \"50.9%\",\n439\t            \"0.920\"\n440\t          ],\n441\t          [\n442\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n443\t            62,\n444\t            34,\n445\t            28,\n446\t            \"54.8%\",\n447\t            \"0.280\"\n448\t          ]\n449\t        ]\n450\t      },\n451\t      {\n452\t        \"title\": \"Table 7: Casual-Original Subset — Formal Win Rate When Opposing Original Preference\",\n453\t        \"columns\": [\n454\t          \"Judge\",\n455\t          \"n_consistent\",\n456\t          \"Formal Wins\",\n457\t          \"Formal WR\",\n458\t          \"p\"\n459\t        ],\n460\t        \"rows\": [\n461\t          [\n462\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n463\t            22,\n464\t            12,\n465\t            \"54.5%\",\n466\t            \"0.832\"\n467\t          ],\n468\t          [\n469\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n470\t            27,\n471\t            17,\n472\t            \"63.0%\",\n473\t            \"0.072†\"\n474\t          ],\n475\t          [\n476\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n477\t            36,\n478\t            22,\n479\t            \"61.1%\",\n480\t            \"0.096†\"\n481\t          ]\n482\t        ],\n483\t        \"footnote\": \"† p<0.10. Formal = rewrite in this subset, so original preference opposes formality.\"\n484\t      }\n485\t    ],\n486\t    \"figures\": [],\n487\t    \"analysis\": \"A6 假设成立：original preference 贡献 <5 个百分点 (mean 53% - 50% = 3%)， 远小于 formality premium (mean 68.5% - 50% = 18.5%)。Casual-original subset 在 Claude (63%) 和 Gemini (61.1%) 上均 >60%，best judge p=0.072 满足 p<0.10。 casual_orig_best_judge_wr 0.63 在 [0.60, 0.70] 范围内。 Direction asymmetry (MVP 中 formal-orig 78.8% vs casual-orig 54.5%) 主要解释 从 \\\"original preference\\\" 转向 \\\"改写方向的非对称难度\\\"。\\n\\n\\nOriginal preference 在所有 judge 上均弱且不显著 (mean 53.0%)，因为 double-rewrite 过程 虽引入轻微 rewrite artifact (如稍微不自然的措辞)，但这个 artifact 对 judge 影响是随机的 而非系统性的。Claude 的 original preference 最弱 (50.9%)，可能因为 Claude 对 \\\"naturalness\\\" 的敏感度更低。Gemini 稍高 (54.8%)，可能因为轻量模型对 fluency 微妙差异更敏感。 Casual-original subset 分析是关键：Claude 上 63.0% formal win rate (p=0.072) 说明即使 formality preference 与 original preference 方向相反 (formal = rewrite)， formality 仍占上风。这在 GPT-4o 上不显著 (54.5%) 可能因为 GPT-4o 的 original preference (53.3%) 与 formality preference 恰好在 casual-original subset 上互相抵消。 Claude original preference 更弱 (50.9%)，所以 formality 更容易 dominate。\\n\"\n488\t  },\n489\t  {\n490\t    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=500)\",\n491\t    \"description\": \"将 formality pairwise 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。选择效应最强的 judge×benchmark 组合 (Gemini×LLMBar)。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。 五个 n=100 子组的稳定性分析。\\n\",\n492\t    \"results\": {\n493\t      \"n_total\": 500,\n494\t      \"n_valid_both_trials\": 490,\n495\t      \"n_consistent\": 278,\n496\t      \"consistency_rate\": 0.567,\n497\t      \"formal_wins\": 184,\n498\t      \"casual_wins\": 94,\n499\t      \"formal_win_rate\": 0.662,\n500\t      \"wilson_ci\": [\n501\t        0.604,\n502\t        0.716\n503\t      ],\n504\t      \"sign_test_p\": 1e-05,\n505\t      \"cohens_h\": 0.337,\n506\t      \"likert_ate_n500\": 0.11,\n507\t      \"likert_ate_p_n500\": 0.082,\n508\t      \"likert_still_borderline\": true,\n509\t      \"sub1_winrate\": 0.7,\n510\t      \"sub2_winrate\": 0.65,\n511\t      \"sub3_winrate\": 0.68,\n512\t      \"sub4_winrate\": 0.64,\n513\t      \"sub5_winrate\": 0.64,\n514\t      \"subgroup_sd\": 0.026,\n515\t      \"power_n100_d065\": 0.72,\n516\t      \"power_n300_d065\": 0.97,\n517\t      \"power_n500_d065\": 0.995,\n518\t      \"min_detectable_wr_n500\": 0.56,\n519\t      \"nli_ge90_n_consistent\": 232,\n520\t      \"nli_ge90_winrate\": 0.685,\n521\t      \"nli_ge80_n_consistent\": 262,\n522\t      \"nli_ge80_winrate\": 0.668\n523\t    },\n524\t    \"tables\": [\n525\t      {\n526\t        \"title\": \"Table 8: Scaled Replication (Gemini × LLMBar, Formality)\",\n527\t        \"columns\": [\n528\t          \"Scale\",\n529\t          \"n_consistent\",\n530\t          \"Formal WR\",\n531\t          \"95% CI\",\n532\t          \"Pairwise p\",\n533\t          \"Likert p\"\n534\t        ],\n535\t        \"rows\": [\n536\t          [\n537\t            \"n=100 (MVP pilot)\",\n538\t            55,\n539\t            \"69.1%\",\n540\t            \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\",\n541\t            \"0.006**\",\n542\t            \"0.332\"\n543\t          ],\n544\t          [\n545\t            \"n=500 (replication)\",\n546\t            278,\n547\t            \"66.2%\",\n548\t            \"[60.4%, 71.6%]\",\n549\t            \"<0.001***\",\n550\t            \"0.082†\"\n551\t          ]\n552\t        ],\n553\t        \"footnote\": \"Likert p still non-significant at n=500 (borderline), confirming structural measurement gap.\"\n554\t      },\n555\t      {\n556\t        \"title\": \"Table 9: Subgroup Stability (5 × n=100 splits)\",\n557\t        \"columns\": [\n558\t          \"Split\",\n559\t          \"n_consistent\",\n560\t          \"Formal WR\"\n561\t        ],\n562\t        \"rows\": [\n563\t          [\n564\t            \"Block 1\",\n565\t            57,\n566\t            \"70.0%\"\n567\t          ],\n568\t          [\n569\t            \"Block 2\",\n570\t            53,\n571\t            \"65.0%\"\n572\t          ],\n573\t          [\n574\t            \"Block 3\",\n575\t            56,\n576\t            \"68.0%\"\n577\t          ],\n578\t          [\n579\t            \"Block 4\",\n580\t            54,\n581\t            \"64.0%\"\n582\t          ],\n583\t          [\n584\t            \"Block 5\",\n585\t            58,\n586\t            \"64.0%\"\n587\t          ],\n588\t          [\n589\t            \"Full n=500\",\n590\t            278,\n591\t            \"66.2%\"\n592\t          ]\n593\t        ]\n594\t      },\n595\t      {\n596\t        \"title\": \"Table 10: Power Analysis\",\n597\t        \"columns\": [\n598\t          \"n\",\n599\t          \"Power (WR=0.65)\",\n600\t          \"Min Detectable WR (power=0.80)\"\n601\t        ],\n602\t        \"rows\": [\n603\t          [\n604\t            100,\n605\t            \"0.72\",\n606\t            \"62.0%\"\n607\t          ],\n608\t          [\n609\t            300,\n610\t            \"0.97\",\n611\t            \"57.5%\"\n612\t          ],\n613\t          [\n614\t            500,\n615\t            \"0.995\",\n616\t            \"56.0%\"\n617\t          ]\n618\t        ]\n619\t      }\n620\t    ],\n621\t    \"figures\": [],\n622\t    \"analysis\": \"n500_formal_win_rate 0.662 在 [0.58, 0.70] 范围内。p<0.001 满足 p<0.01 核心假设。 n=500 Likert 仍 borderline (p=0.082) 是 C2 的额外弹药——即使 5× sample size 都不能 让 Likert 检测到 pairwise 在 n=100 就发现的效应。Power analysis 解释了 why： pairwise within-subject design 的 effective sample size 远大于 Likert between-subject。\\n\\n\\nn=500 时 win rate 0.662 相比 n=100 pilot 的 0.691 有 2.9% 的 regression to mean， 这在预期范围内——pilot 的 point estimate 在 CI [0.56, 0.80] 上端，larger sample 收敛到 true effect。CI 从 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.60, 0.72]，p 从 0.006 降到 <0.001。 五个 n=100 子组 win rate 在 0.64-0.70 范围波动 (σ=0.026)，展示效应高度稳定。 关键发现：即使 n=500，Likert ATE 仍仅 borderline 显著 (p=0.082)——这强化了 C2： Likert blindspot 不是 power 问题，而是 measurement sensitivity 的结构性差异。 如果仅仅是 power 问题，n=500 的 Likert 应当显著；它仍不显著说明 Likert 对 style bias 的检测本身就是 structurally impaired。\\n\"\n623\t  },\n624\t  {\n625\t    \"name\": \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\",\n626\t    \"description\": \"第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变词汇和句法 但不改变信息内容。Full pipeline: counterfactual gen → NLI verification → dual-direction pairwise scoring。三个 judge × LLMBar，n=100。\\n\",\n627\t    \"results\": {\n628\t      \"register_nli_pass_rate\": 0.86,\n629\t      \"register_nli_mean\": 0.893,\n630\t      \"register_bertscore_mean\": 0.839,\n631\t      \"register_both_pass\": 0.83,\n632\t      \"gpt4o_academic_win_rate\": 0.66,\n633\t      \"gpt4o_n_consistent\": 53,\n634\t      \"gpt4o_p\": 0.015,\n635\t      \"claude_academic_win_rate\": 0.62,\n636\t      \"claude_n_consistent\": 50,\n637\t      \"claude_p\": 0.042,\n638\t      \"gemini_academic_win_rate\": 0.714,\n639\t      \"gemini_n_consistent\": 56,\n640\t      \"gemini_p\": 0.003,\n641\t      \"judges_significant\": 3,\n642\t      \"mean_academic_winrate\": 0.665,\n643\t      \"gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.289,\n644\t      \"claude_likert_p\": 0.511,\n645\t      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.167,\n646\t      \"register_likert_pairwise_gap\": true\n647\t    },\n648\t    \"tables\": [\n649\t      {\n650\t        \"title\": \"Table A2: Register (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\",\n651\t        \"columns\": [\n652\t          \"Judge\",\n653\t          \"n_consistent\",\n654\t          \"Academic Wins\",\n655\t          \"Conv. Wins\",\n656\t          \"Win Rate\",\n657\t          \"Pairwise p\",\n658\t          \"Likert p\"\n659\t        ],\n660\t        \"rows\": [\n661\t          [\n662\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n663\t            53,\n664\t            35,\n665\t            18,\n666\t            \"66.0%\",\n667\t            \"0.015*\",\n668\t            \"0.289\"\n669\t          ],\n670\t          [\n671\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n672\t            50,\n673\t            31,\n674\t            19,\n675\t            \"62.0%\",\n676\t            \"0.042*\",\n677\t            \"0.511\"\n678\t          ],\n679\t          [\n680\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n681\t            56,\n682\t            40,\n683\t            16,\n684\t            \"71.4%\",\n685\t            \"0.003**\",\n686\t            \"0.167\"\n687\t          ]\n688\t        ]\n689\t      },\n690\t      {\n691\t        \"title\": \"Table A3: Cross-Axis Summary (LLMBar, 3 judges)\",\n692\t        \"columns\": [\n693\t          \"Axis\",\n694\t          \"Mean WR\",\n695\t          \"Judges Sig. (3)\",\n696\t          \"NLI Pass\",\n697\t          \"Likert Detects?\"\n698\t        ],\n699\t        \"rows\": [\n700\t          [\n701\t            \"Formality\",\n702\t            \"68.5%\",\n703\t            \"3/3\",\n704\t            \"88%\",\n705\t            \"0/3\"\n706\t          ],\n707\t          [\n708\t            \"Register\",\n709\t            \"66.5%\",\n710\t            \"3/3\",\n711\t            \"86%\",\n712\t            \"0/3\"\n713\t          ],\n714\t          [\n715\t            \"Tone\",\n716\t            \"—\",\n717\t            \"—\",\n718\t            \"65% (failed)\",\n719\t            \"N/A\"\n720\t          ],\n721\t          [\n722\t            \"Verbosity\",\n723\t            \"—\",\n724\t            \"—\",\n725\t            \"65% (failed)\",\n726\t            \"N/A\"\n727\t          ]\n728\t        ]\n729\t      }\n730\t    ],\n731\t    \"figures\": [],\n732\t    \"analysis\": \"Register 作为第二个 working axis 将 C3 从 \\\"only formality works\\\" 提升为 \\\"content-preserving surface-level axes generally work\\\"。效应量级系统性排序 formality > register > (tone/verbosity failed)，与 linguistic level 数量正相关： formality 跨词汇+句法+语用，register 跨词汇+句法，tone 主要在语用层。 这提供了 principled taxonomy：改变 surface form 而不改变 information content 或 epistemic commitment 的 axes 适用于 CSD。\\n\\n\\nRegister (academic vs conversational) 是 surface-level 词汇+句法变换，不改变信息内容： Latinate 术语 vs everyday words, 复杂从句 vs 简单句, disciplinary jargon vs lay terms。 效应在 formality 和 tone 之间 (mean 0.665)，因为 register 涉及词汇和句法层面变化 但比 formality 更窄——formality 包含 register + tone + 其他 cues 的 composite。 NLI pass 0.86 略低于 formality (0.88)，因为 academic vocabulary 有时引入微妙语义偏移 (术语替代 layman terms 可能 shift specificity)。Judge 梯度保持 Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude， 进一步确认这是 judge 内在属性而非 axis-specific 现象。所有 Likert p 均不显著， 扩展了 C2 blindspot evidence 到第二个 axis。\\n\"\n733\t  },\n734\t  {\n735\t    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n736\t    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为替代 rewriter，对 LLMBar formality 运行完整 pipeline。 与 Qwen3-32B 结果比较，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。GPT-4o 作为 judge。\\n\",\n737\t    \"results\": {\n738\t      \"llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n739\t      \"llama_nli_mean\": 0.881,\n740\t      \"llama_bertscore_mean\": 0.836,\n741\t      \"llama_n_consistent\": 52,\n742\t      \"llama_formal_win_rate\": 0.66,\n743\t      \"llama_sign_test_p\": 0.015,\n744\t      \"qwen_nli_pass_rate\": 0.88,\n745\t      \"qwen_formal_win_rate\": 0.691,\n746\t      \"qwen_sign_test_p\": 0.006,\n747\t      \"winrate_difference\": 0.031,\n748\t      \"fisher_exact_p_for_difference\": 0.42,\n749\t      \"rewriter_effect_significant\": false\n750\t    },\n751\t    \"tables\": [\n752\t      {\n753\t        \"title\": \"Table A4: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality)\",\n754\t        \"columns\": [\n755\t          \"Rewriter\",\n756\t          \"NLI Pass\",\n757\t          \"Formal WR\",\n758\t          \"Pairwise p\",\n759\t          \"n_consistent\"\n760\t        ],\n761\t        \"rows\": [\n762\t          [\n763\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n764\t            \"88%\",\n765\t            \"69.1%\",\n766\t            \"0.006**\",\n767\t            55\n768\t          ],\n769\t          [\n770\t            \"Llama-3.1-70B\",\n771\t            \"85%\",\n772\t            \"66.0%\",\n773\t            \"0.015*\",\n774\t            52\n775\t          ],\n776\t          [\n777\t            \"Difference\",\n778\t            \"-3%\",\n779\t            \"-3.1%\",\n780\t            \"Fisher p=0.42\",\n781\t            \"—\"\n782\t          ]\n783\t        ]\n784\t      }\n785\t    ],\n786\t    \"figures\": [],\n787\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix 级实验，但对 reviewer 质疑 rewriter choice 时提供决定性回应。 两个不同 family 的 rewriter 产生一致的 formality premium，确认效应的 robustness。\\n\\n\\nLlama rewriter 产生略低但仍显著的 formality premium (0.66 vs 0.69)，差异不显著 (Fisher p=0.42)。NLI pass rate 略低 (0.85 vs 0.88) 因为 Llama-70B 在 instruction following 上略弱于 Qwen3-32B (后者受益于 Qwen3 的强 instruction tuning)，导致少量 counterfactual 有轻微语义偏移。3% win rate 差异在统计噪声范围内，排除了 \\\"Qwen rewriter 引入某种被 judge 偏好的 writing pattern\\\" 的 confound。 关键论点：formality bias 检测不依赖于特定 rewriter family。\\n\"\n788\t  },\n789\t  {\n790\t    \"name\": \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\",\n791\t    \"description\": \"DREAM CRITICAL。对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 sign test：每对中 formal version 的 Likert score 是否严格高于 casual version？如果 binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 是 test choice 差异，非 measurement method 差异。如果不显著 → 确认 C2。 零成本重分析。\\n\",\n792\t    \"results\": {\n793\t      \"data_source\": \"scored_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar, n=88 primary)\",\n794\t      \"n_primary\": 88,\n795\t      \"n_formal_higher\": 29,\n796\t      \"n_casual_higher\": 21,\n797\t      \"n_tied\": 38,\n798\t      \"tie_fraction\": 0.432,\n799\t      \"n_non_tied\": 50,\n800\t      \"binarized_formal_rate\": 0.58,\n801\t      \"sign_test_p\": 0.24,\n802\t      \"is_significant\": false,\n803\t      \"strict_binarize_diff_ge2\": {\n804\t        \"n_non_tied\": 18,\n805\t        \"formal_wins\": 11,\n806\t        \"sign_test_p\": 0.48\n807\t      },\n808\t      \"pairwise_formal_wr\": 0.691,\n809\t      \"pairwise_p\": 0.006,\n810\t      \"gap_confirmed\": true\n811\t    },\n812\t    \"tables\": [\n813\t      {\n814\t        \"title\": \"Table 11: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise — C2 Decisive Test\",\n815\t        \"columns\": [\n816\t          \"Method\",\n817\t          \"n (non-tied/consistent)\",\n818\t          \"Formal Rate\",\n819\t          \"Sign Test p\",\n820\t          \"Conclusion\"\n821\t        ],\n822\t        \"rows\": [\n823\t          [\n824\t            \"Pairwise (position-controlled)\",\n825\t            55,\n826\t            \"69.1%\",\n827\t            \"0.006**\",\n828\t            \"Significant bias detected\"\n829\t          ],\n830\t          [\n831\t            \"Binarized Likert (score > comparison)\",\n832\t            50,\n833\t            \"58.0%\",\n834\t            \"0.240\",\n835\t            \"Not significant\"\n836\t          ],\n837\t          [\n838\t            \"Binarized Likert (diff ≥ 2)\",\n839\t            18,\n840\t            \"61.1%\",\n841\t            \"0.481\",\n842\t            \"Not significant\"\n843\t          ]\n844\t        ],\n845\t        \"footnote\": \"Same underlying data (scored_32b.jsonl). Pairwise detects what binarized Likert misses.\"\n846\t      }\n847\t    ],\n848\t    \"figures\": [],\n849\t    \"analysis\": \"THIS IS THE DECISIVE EVIDENCE FOR C2。binarized_likert_sign_p = 0.24 在 [0.12, 1.0] 范围内。 排除了 \\\"Likert 和 Pairwise 用不同 statistical test 所以不可比\\\" 的 alternative explanation。 现在三种分析都使用 sign test on binary outcome，唯一差异是 measurement method： (1) Pairwise forced-choice → 69.1%, p=0.006 (2) Binarized Likert score comparison → 58.0%, p=0.24 (3) Raw Likert ATE → p=0.33 Pairwise 胜出是因为它消除了 Likert 的 tie problem (43% tied) 和 between-item calibration noise。 Main Result Table 中增加 Binarized Likert 列是 C2 的命门证据。\\n\\n\\nBinarized Likert 不显著 (p=0.24) 的根因是 Likert scale 的 discretization loss。 在 1-10 量表上，formality 引入的 quality perception 差异约 0.10 分 (从 Likert ATE)， 这远小于一个 scale step。因此 43.2% 的 pair 获得相同 Likert score (tied)——这些 pair 中 judge 确实感知到了 formality 差异 (pairwise 中会做出选择)，但 Likert 的 粗粒度量表无法捕捉这个差异。在 50 个 non-tied pairs 中，formal 略占优 (58%) 但 sample size 太小 (n=50 而非 pairwise 的 n=55 consistent)，sign test power 不足。 即使用更严格的 binarization (score difference ≥ 2)，n 降到 18，formal 11/18 (61%) 但 p=0.48 更加不显著。关键 insight: pairwise 的 forced-choice 消除了 tie 问题—— judge 必须在两个版本间选择，将 Likert 中被 tie 掩盖的微弱偏好显现出来。 这证明 Likert-Pairwise gap 是 measurement granularity 差异，非 statistical test 选择差异。\\n\"\n850\t  },\n851\t  {\n852\t    \"name\": \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\",\n853\t    \"description\": \"在 70%, 75%, 80%, 85%, 90%, 95% 六个 NLI threshold 上重新计算 formality pairwise results。 验证结论对 threshold 选择的 robustness。零成本重分析已有 pairwise_32b 数据。\\n\",\n854\t    \"results\": {\n855\t      \"data_source\": \"pairwise_results_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\",\n856\t      \"thresholds\": {\n857\t        \"nli_70\": {\n858\t          \"n_pairs_pass\": 96,\n859\t          \"n_consistent\": 53,\n860\t          \"formal_wins\": 37,\n861\t          \"formal_wr\": 0.698,\n862\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.005\n863\t        },\n864\t        \"nli_75\": {\n865\t          \"n_pairs_pass\": 94,\n866\t          \"n_consistent\": 52,\n867\t          \"formal_wins\": 36,\n868\t          \"formal_wr\": 0.692,\n869\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.006\n870\t        },\n871\t        \"nli_80\": {\n872\t          \"n_pairs_pass\": 88,\n873\t          \"n_consistent\": 50,\n874\t          \"formal_wins\": 35,\n875\t          \"formal_wr\": 0.7,\n876\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.005\n877\t        },\n878\t        \"nli_85\": {\n879\t          \"n_pairs_pass\": 72,\n880\t          \"n_consistent\": 42,\n881\t          \"formal_wins\": 31,\n882\t          \"formal_wr\": 0.738,\n883\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.003\n884\t        },\n885\t        \"nli_90\": {\n886\t          \"n_pairs_pass\": 52,\n887\t          \"n_consistent\": 46,\n888\t          \"formal_wins\": 34,\n889\t          \"formal_wr\": 0.739,\n890\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.002\n891\t        },\n892\t        \"nli_95\": {\n893\t          \"n_pairs_pass\": 36,\n894\t          \"n_consistent\": 28,\n895\t          \"formal_wins\": 21,\n896\t          \"formal_wr\": 0.75,\n897\t          \"sign_test_p\": 0.013\n898\t        }\n899\t      },\n900\t      \"all_significant_70_to_95\": true,\n901\t      \"winrate_trend\": \"monotonically increasing (0.698 → 0.750)\",\n902\t      \"p_value_trend\": \"decreasing then increasing (0.005 → 0.002 → 0.013) due to n tradeoff\",\n903\t      \"significant_range\": \"70%-95%\"\n904\t    },\n905\t    \"tables\": [\n906\t      {\n907\t        \"title\": \"Table 12: NLI Threshold Sensitivity (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality Pairwise)\",\n908\t        \"columns\": [\n909\t          \"NLI Threshold\",\n910\t          \"n_pass\",\n911\t          \"n_consistent\",\n912\t          \"Formal WR\",\n913\t          \"Sign Test p\"\n914\t        ],\n915\t        \"rows\": [\n916\t          [\n917\t            \"≥70%\",\n918\t            96,\n919\t            53,\n920\t            \"69.8%\",\n921\t            \"0.005**\"\n922\t          ],\n923\t          [\n924\t            \"≥75%\",\n925\t            94,\n926\t            52,\n927\t            \"69.2%\",\n928\t            \"0.006**\"\n929\t          ],\n930\t          [\n931\t            \"≥80%\",\n932\t            88,\n933\t            50,\n934\t            \"70.0%\",\n935\t            \"0.005**\"\n936\t          ],\n937\t          [\n938\t            \"≥85%\",\n939\t            72,\n940\t            42,\n941\t            \"73.8%\",\n942\t            \"0.003**\"\n943\t          ],\n944\t          [\n945\t            \"≥90%\",\n946\t            52,\n947\t            46,\n948\t            \"73.9%\",\n949\t            \"0.002**\"\n950\t          ],\n951\t          [\n952\t            \"≥95%\",\n953\t            36,\n954\t            28,\n955\t            \"75.0%\",\n956\t            \"0.013*\"\n957\t          ]\n958\t        ],\n959\t        \"footnote\": \"All thresholds from 70% to 95% yield significant results. Default threshold: 80%.\"\n960\t      }\n961\t    ],\n962\t    \"figures\": [],\n963\t    \"analysis\": \"nli_threshold_sensitivity_significant_range = ['70%-95%']，完美匹配核心假设。 结论不依赖 threshold 选择——从最宽松 (70%) 到最严格 (95%) 均显著。 Win rate 随 threshold 上升这一 monotonic trend 说明 content preservation quality 与 formality effect purity 正相关，支持 CSD 的 causal interpretation。\\n\\n\\nFormality effect 在所有 NLI threshold 上均显著，因为 formality 改写是高质量的 surface-level 变换——即使在宽松 threshold (70%) 下加入的额外 pairs 中有一些 semantic drift， formality premium 仍然 dominant。Win rate 随 threshold 提高而单调递增 (0.698→0.750)， 说明 cleaner pairs (higher NLI) 的 formality effect 更纯——content preservation 越好， observed bias 越接近 true causal effect。p 值在 85-90% 处最低 (0.002)，因为此处 n (42-46) 与 effect size (0.74) 达到最佳平衡；95% threshold 下 n 降到 28， 尽管 effect size 最高 (0.75)，power 损失导致 p 略升至 0.013，但仍远低于 0.05。 Tone 的 NLI 在 72% 处 borderline——sensitivity analysis 显示即使在 70% threshold 下 formality 仍稳健，这不是 threshold tuning 的结果。\\n\"\n964\t  },\n965\t  {\n966\t    \"name\": \"Consistency filter bias analysis\",\n967\t    \"description\": \"比较 position-consistent pairs vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text lengths、 task types，检查 42-52% 的 discard rate 是否引入系统性偏差。零成本重分析。\\n\",\n968\t    \"results\": {\n969\t      \"data_source\": \"pairwise_results_32b.jsonl\",\n970\t      \"total_valid_pairs\": 98,\n971\t      \"n_consistent\": 55,\n972\t      \"n_inconsistent\": 43,\n973\t      \"discard_rate\": 0.439,\n974\t      \"consistent_nli_mean\": 0.903,\n975\t      \"inconsistent_nli_mean\": 0.886,\n976\t      \"nli_ttest_p\": 0.42,\n977\t      \"nli_difference_significant\": false,\n978\t      \"consistent_text_length_mean\": 142.3,\n979\t      \"inconsistent_text_length_mean\": 137.8,\n980\t      \"length_ttest_p\": 0.58,\n981\t      \"length_difference_significant\": false,\n982\t      \"consistent_formal_orig_fraction\": 0.6,\n983\t      \"inconsistent_formal_orig_fraction\": 0.558,\n984\t      \"orig_style_chi2_p\": 0.67,\n985\t      \"orig_style_difference_significant\": false,\n986\t      \"consistent_bertscore_mean\": 0.848,\n987\t      \"inconsistent_bertscore_mean\": 0.834,\n988\t      \"bertscore_ttest_p\": 0.38,\n989\t      \"bertscore_difference_significant\": false,\n990\t      \"task_type_chi2_p\": 0.73,\n991\t      \"task_type_difference_significant\": false,\n992\t      \"any_significant_difference\": false,\n993\t      \"filter_introduces_bias\": false\n994\t    },\n995\t    \"tables\": [\n996\t      {\n997\t        \"title\": \"Table A5: Consistency Filter Bias Analysis (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\",\n998\t        \"columns\": [\n999\t          \"Property\",\n1000\t          \"Consistent (n=55)\",\n1001\t          \"Inconsistent (n=43)\",\n1002\t          \"Test\",\n1003\t          \"p\"\n1004\t        ],\n1005\t        \"rows\": [\n1006\t          [\n1007\t            \"NLI Mean\",\n1008\t            \"0.903\",\n1009\t            \"0.886\",\n1010\t            \"t-test\",\n1011\t            \"0.42\"\n1012\t          ],\n1013\t          [\n1014\t            \"Text Length (words)\",\n1015\t            \"142.3\",\n1016\t            \"137.8\",\n1017\t            \"t-test\",\n1018\t            \"0.58\"\n1019\t          ],\n1020\t          [\n1021\t            \"BERTScore Mean\",\n1022\t            \"0.848\",\n1023\t            \"0.834\",\n1024\t            \"t-test\",\n1025\t            \"0.38\"\n1026\t          ],\n1027\t          [\n1028\t            \"Formal-Original %\",\n1029\t            \"60.0%\",\n1030\t            \"55.8%\",\n1031\t            \"χ²\",\n1032\t            \"0.67\"\n1033\t          ],\n1034\t          [\n1035\t            \"Task Type Distribution\",\n1036\t            \"—\",\n1037\t            \"—\",\n1038\t            \"χ²\",\n1039\t            \"0.73\"\n1040\t          ]\n1041\t        ],\n1042\t        \"footnote\": \"No significant differences. Consistency filtering does not systematically bias the retained sample.\"\n1043\t      }\n1044\t    ],\n1045\t    \"figures\": [],\n1046\t    \"analysis\": \"所有 5 个 comparison 均不显著 (最小 p=0.38)，conclusively 排除 systematic filter bias。 42-52% 的 discard rate 虽高，但 discarded pairs 与 retained pairs 在 observables 上 indistinguishable。Reviewer 对 \\\"high discard rate → biased sample\\\" 的 concern 可用此表直接回应。建议放在 Appendix 作为 methodological robustness check。\\n\\n\\nPosition-consistency filtering 不引入系统性偏差，因为 position inconsistency 的主要来源 是 judge 的 confidence 而非 pair 的 systematic properties。Judge 对某些 pairs 有明确偏好 (无论位置如何都选同一个) → consistent，对另一些 pairs 犹豫不决 (位置影响选择) → inconsistent。 犹豫不决与 pair 的 NLI、text length、task type 无关，而与 quality 差异的微妙程度有关—— 当两个版本在 judge 眼中 \\\"差不多好\\\" 时，position 成为 tie-breaker。这是随机噪声， 不是对特定类型 pair 的系统性过滤。NLI 略高 (0.903 vs 0.886) 但 p=0.42 不显著， 说明 content preservation 质量不驱动 consistency。consistent pairs 中 formal-original fraction (0.60) 略高于 inconsistent (0.56)，但差异远不显著 (p=0.67)，排除了 \\\"filtering selects for original-preference-aligned pairs\\\" 的 confound。\\n\"\n1047\t  },\n1048\t  {\n1049\t    \"name\": \"Human NLI validation (80 annotations)\",\n1050\t    \"description\": \"Human validation of NLI gate decisions。对 80 个 counterfactual pairs 做人工标注： content 是否 preserved。报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen's κ)。 可使用 LLM-as-annotator (GPT-4) + human spot check 的混合策略。\\n\",\n1051\t    \"results\": {\n1052\t      \"n_annotated\": 80,\n1053\t      \"n_nli_high\": 50,\n1054\t      \"n_nli_low\": 30,\n1055\t      \"human_preserved\": 62,\n1056\t      \"human_not_preserved\": 18,\n1057\t      \"human_preservation_rate\": 0.775,\n1058\t      \"nli_preserved\": 58,\n1059\t      \"nli_not_preserved\": 22,\n1060\t      \"both_preserved\": 54,\n1061\t      \"both_not_preserved\": 14,\n1062\t      \"nli_preserved_human_not\": 4,\n1063\t      \"nli_not_preserved_human_yes\": 8,\n1064\t      \"raw_agreement\": 0.85,\n1065\t      \"cohens_kappa\": 0.72,\n1066\t      \"kappa_interpretation\": \"substantial agreement\",\n1067\t      \"nli_false_positive_rate\": 0.069,\n1068\t      \"nli_false_negative_rate\": 0.129,\n1069\t      \"false_positive_pattern\": \"subtle information additions in formal rewrites that NLI misses\",\n1070\t      \"false_negative_pattern\": \"stylistic paraphrases that NLI over-penalizes as semantic change\"\n1071\t    },\n1072\t    \"tables\": [\n1073\t      {\n1074\t        \"title\": \"Table A6: Human-NLI Agreement on Content Preservation (n=80)\",\n1075\t        \"columns\": [\n1076\t          \"\",\n1077\t          \"Human: Preserved\",\n1078\t          \"Human: Not Preserved\",\n1079\t          \"Total\"\n1080\t        ],\n1081\t        \"rows\": [\n1082\t          [\n1083\t            \"NLI: Preserved (≥0.80)\",\n1084\t            54,\n1085\t            4,\n1086\t            58\n1087\t          ],\n1088\t          [\n1089\t            \"NLI: Not Preserved (<0.80)\",\n1090\t            8,\n1091\t            14,\n1092\t            22\n1093\t          ],\n1094\t          [\n1095\t            \"Total\",\n1096\t            62,\n1097\t            18,\n1098\t            80\n1099\t          ]\n1100\t        ],\n1101\t        \"footnote\": \"Cohen's κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement). NLI FPR = 6.9%, FNR = 12.9%.\"\n1102\t      }\n1103\t    ],\n1104\t    \"figures\": [],\n1105\t    \"analysis\": \"κ = 0.72 在 [0.61, 0.80] \\\"substantial\\\" 范围内，满足审稿人对 NLI gate 可信度的要求。 NLI 偏保守 (FNR > FPR) 对 CSD 有利：retained pairs 的 content preservation 质量 被 underestimate 而非 overestimate。建议论文中强调：\\\"NLI false positives are rare (6.9%), meaning pairs that pass the gate genuinely preserve content.\\\"\\n\\n\\nCohen's κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement) 因为 NLI 模型 (DeBERTa-large-MNLI) 的 training data 与 content preservation 判断高度对齐——NLI 本质上就是判断两个文本是否表达相同信息， 这与 \\\"counterfactual 是否保持 content\\\" 的判断完全一致。False positive rate 低 (6.9%) 说明 NLI gate 通过的 pairs 绝大多数确实 content-preserved——这是 CSD 结论可信度的基础。 False negative rate 较高 (12.9%) 说明 NLI 偏保守 (over-reject)，但这对 CSD 是安全的方向： over-rejection 意味着 retained pairs 的 content preservation 质量比 NLI score 建议的更高。 8 个 false negative 主要是 stylistic paraphrasing (如换用近义词或调整句子结构) 被 NLI 判为 non-entailment，但人工判断这些改变不影响信息内容。\\n\"\n1106\t  },\n1107\t  {\n1108\t    \"name\": \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\",\n1109\t    \"description\": \"Logistic regression 正式分离 formality 和 original preference。 Pool exp-001/002 所有 judge×benchmark pairwise 数据。DV: formal_preferred (1/0)。 IV: is_formal_original (1/0), judge (fixed effects), benchmark (fixed effects)。 Test formality 主效应 (intercept) 是否显著，interaction 是否不显著。\\n\",\n1110\t    \"results\": {\n1111\t      \"data_source\": \"pooled pairwise from all judge × benchmark combinations\",\n1112\t      \"n_observations\": 459,\n1113\t      \"intercept_beta\": 0.52,\n1114\t      \"intercept_se\": 0.19,\n1115\t      \"intercept_z\": 2.74,\n1116\t      \"intercept_p\": 0.006,\n1117\t      \"intercept_odds_ratio\": 1.68,\n1118\t      \"intercept_interpretation\": \"formal 被偏好的 odds 是 casual 的 1.68 倍，controlling for original status\",\n1119\t      \"is_formal_original_beta\": 0.34,\n1120\t      \"is_formal_original_se\": 0.17,\n1121\t      \"is_formal_original_z\": 2.0,\n1122\t      \"is_formal_original_p\": 0.046,\n1123\t      \"is_formal_original_or\": 1.4,\n1124\t      \"interaction_beta\": 0.12,\n1125\t      \"interaction_se\": 0.22,\n1126\t      \"interaction_z\": 0.55,\n1127\t      \"interaction_p\": 0.58,\n1128\t      \"interaction_significant\": false,\n1129\t      \"judge_claude_beta\": -0.28,\n1130\t      \"judge_claude_p\": 0.11,\n1131\t      \"judge_gemini_beta\": 0.19,\n1132\t      \"judge_gemini_p\": 0.24,\n1133\t      \"benchmark_alpacaeval_beta\": -0.08,\n1134\t      \"benchmark_alpacaeval_p\": 0.62,\n1135\t      \"benchmark_mtbench_beta\": -0.15,\n1136\t      \"benchmark_mtbench_p\": 0.38,\n1137\t      \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.042,\n1138\t      \"aic\": 582.3,\n1139\t      \"bic\": 611.7,\n1140\t      \"raw_mean_formal_wr\": 0.664,\n1141\t      \"original_preference_contribution\": 0.033,\n1142\t      \"csd_adjusted_formal_wr\": 0.631,\n1143\t      \"logistic_formality_coef_p\": 0.006\n1144\t    },\n1145\t    \"tables\": [\n1146\t      {\n1147\t        \"title\": \"Table 13: Logistic Regression — Formality vs Original Preference Decomposition\",\n1148\t        \"columns\": [\n1149\t          \"Predictor\",\n1150\t          \"β\",\n1151\t          \"SE\",\n1152\t          \"z\",\n1153\t          \"p\",\n1154\t          \"Odds Ratio\"\n1155\t        ],\n1156\t        \"rows\": [\n1157\t          [\n1158\t            \"Intercept (formality effect)\",\n1159\t            \"0.52\",\n1160\t            \"0.19\",\n1161\t            \"2.74\",\n1162\t            \"0.006**\",\n1163\t            \"1.68\"\n1164\t          ],\n1165\t          [\n1166\t            \"is_formal_original\",\n1167\t            \"0.34\",\n1168\t            \"0.17\",\n1169\t            \"2.00\",\n1170\t            \"0.046*\",\n1171\t            \"1.40\"\n1172\t          ],\n1173\t          [\n1174\t            \"Interaction\",\n1175\t            \"0.12\",\n1176\t            \"0.22\",\n1177\t            \"0.55\",\n1178\t            \"0.583\",\n1179\t            \"1.13\"\n1180\t          ],\n1181\t          [\n1182\t            \"Judge: Claude (vs GPT-4o)\",\n1183\t            \"-0.28\",\n1184\t            \"0.17\",\n1185\t            \"-1.65\",\n1186\t            \"0.110\",\n1187\t            \"0.76\"\n1188\t          ],\n1189\t          [\n1190\t            \"Judge: Gemini (vs GPT-4o)\",\n1191\t            \"0.19\",\n1192\t            \"0.16\",\n1193\t            \"1.19\",\n1194\t            \"0.240\",\n1195\t            \"1.21\"\n1196\t          ],\n1197\t          [\n1198\t            \"Bench: AlpacaEval (vs LLMBar)\",\n1199\t            \"-0.08\",\n1200\t            \"0.16\",\n1201\t            \"-0.50\",\n1202\t            \"0.620\",\n1203\t            \"0.92\"\n1204\t          ],\n1205\t          [\n1206\t            \"Bench: MT-Bench (vs LLMBar)\",\n1207\t            \"-0.15\",\n1208\t            \"0.17\",\n1209\t            \"-0.88\",\n1210\t            \"0.380\",\n1211\t            \"0.86\"\n1212\t          ]\n1213\t        ],\n1214\t        \"footnote\": \"N=459 observations pooled across 9 judge×benchmark combinations. McFadden R²=0.042.\"\n1215\t      },\n1216\t      {\n1217\t        \"title\": \"Table 14: CSD-Adjusted Win Rate\",\n1218\t        \"columns\": [\n1219\t          \"Metric\",\n1220\t          \"Value\",\n1221\t          \"Source\"\n1222\t        ],\n1223\t        \"rows\": [\n1224\t          [\n1225\t            \"Raw formal win rate (mean across combos)\",\n1226\t            \"66.4%\",\n1227\t            \"exp-001/002\"\n1228\t          ],\n1229\t          [\n1230\t            \"Original preference contribution\",\n1231\t            \"+3.3%\",\n1232\t            \"exp-014 β₁\"\n1233\t          ],\n1234\t          [\n1235\t            \"CSD-adjusted formal win rate\",\n1236\t            \"63.1%\",\n1237\t            \"Raw − original contribution\"\n1238\t          ],\n1239\t          [\n1240\t            \"95% CI of adjusted rate\",\n1241\t            \"[57.2%, 69.0%]\",\n1242\t            \"Bootstrap\"\n1243\t          ]\n1244\t        ]\n1245\t      }\n1246\t    ],\n1247\t    \"figures\": [],\n1248\t    \"analysis\": \"logistic_formality_coef_p = 0.006 在 [0.001, 0.05] 范围内。Interaction p = 0.58 明确不显著。C4 (practical guidance) 有了统计基础：CSD-adjusted win rate 公式为 adjusted_wr = raw_wr - β₁/(β₀+β₁) × (raw_wr - 0.50)。这比 ad-hoc additive correction 更有统计根据。Paper 可以给出 practitioner checklist：(1) use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit; (2) run RATE control to quantify original preference; (3) report both raw and CSD-adjusted win rates; (4) verify content preservation per axis before applying CSD。\\n\\nFormality 主效应 (intercept β₀=0.52, p=0.006) 显著，说明控制 original status 后 formal 仍被系统性偏好——这是 formality bias 作为 independent causal effect 的统计证据。 is_formal_original (β₁=0.34, p=0.046) 边缘显著，说明 original preference 确实存在 但效应量 (OR=1.40) 远小于 formality (OR=1.68)。关键：interaction term 不显著 (p=0.58)， 意味着 formality 的效应不依赖于 formal 版本是否为 original——无论 formal 是原文还是改写， judge 都偏好它。这彻底回应了 \\\"observed formality bias 只是 original preference 的 proxy\\\" 的 alternative explanation。Judge 和 benchmark fixed effects 不显著，说明 formality premium 在不同 judge 和 benchmark 间是 stable 的 (尽管 magnitude 有差异， 但 direction 一致)。CSD-adjusted formal win rate = 63.1% (扣除 original preference 贡献 3.3 个百分点)，这是对 reviewer 最保守友好的 headline number。\\n\"\n1249\t  }\n1250\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5aa0c8c7-3106-45b4-8f25-1fa80e0cc92a","uuid":"c6ff77da-764e-49fa-9a19-dee2c0ce00e5","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:03:51.733Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T233719/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。 使用已生成的 counterfactual pairs (n=100)，每个 judge 做 dual-direction pairwise， position control。与 GPT-4o baseline (69.1%, p=0.006) 对比。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_formal_win_rate\": 0.691,\n      \"gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.006,\n      \"gpt4o_n_consistent\": 55,\n      \"gpt4o_formal_wins\": 38,\n      \"gpt4o_casual_wins\": 17,\n      \"claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate\": 0.64,\n      \"claude_sonnet_sign_test_p\": 0.028,\n      \"claude_sonnet_n_consistent\": 50,\n      \"claude_sonnet_formal_wins\": 32,\n      \"claude_sonnet_casual_wins\": 18,\n      \"claude_sonnet_consistency_rate\": 0.51,\n      \"gemini_flash_formal_win_rate\": 0.724,\n      \"gemini_flash_sign_test_p\": 0.002,\n      \"gemini_flash_n_consistent\": 58,\n      \"gemini_flash_formal_wins\": 42,\n      \"gemini_flash_casual_wins\": 16,\n      \"gemini_flash_consistency_rate\": 0.59,\n      \"n_judges_significant_after_holm\": 3,\n      \"holm_corrected_p_values\": {\n        \"gemini\": 0.006,\n        \"gpt4o\": 0.012,\n        \"claude\": 0.028\n      },\n      \"cross_judge_mean_winrate\": 0.685,\n      \"cross_judge_winrate_range\": [\n        0.64,\n        0.724\n      ],\n      \"cross_judge_pairwise_p_median\": 0.006\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 2: Formality Pairwise Results Across Judges (LLMBar, n=100)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Formal Wins\",\n          \"Casual Wins\",\n          \"Win Rate\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Sign Test p\",\n          \"Holm p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            55,\n            38,\n            17,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            \"0.012*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            50,\n            32,\n            18,\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"[50.1%, 75.9%]\",\n            \"0.028*\",\n            \"0.028*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            58,\n            42,\n            16,\n            \"72.4%\",\n            \"[59.8%, 82.3%]\",\n            \"0.002**\",\n            \"0.006**\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"A1 假设成立：3/3 judge 在 Holm correction 后显著。cross_judge_mean_winrate 0.685 在 [0.60, 0.75] 范围中上。Judge 间量级差异 (Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定， 为 C3 axis-dependency 提供 judge 维度证据。Direction asymmetry 在所有 judge 上存在 (formal-original 方向更强)，为 exp-005 original preference 控制提供动机。\\n\\n\\nFormality bias 是 LLM judge 的通用现象而非 GPT-4o 特有。三个 judge 的 RLHF 训练数据 普遍偏向 formal/professional 风格回答，formal text 与 higher-quality content 在 pretraining 语料中高度相关。Claude-Sonnet 效应略弱 (0.64) 因为 Anthropic 的 RLHF 有更多 helpfulness 导向校准，对 surface style 依赖稍低；Gemini-Flash 效应略强 (0.72) 因为轻量模型更依赖 surface heuristics 作为 quality proxy。三者量级差异 (0.64-0.72) 本身也是 C3 evidence—— bias magnitude 是 judge-dependent 的。Holm correction 后全部 p<0.05，因为每个 judge 的 raw p 都足够小 (最大 0.028)，3 重比较惩罚不足以翻转。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD 流程。新 counterfactual generation (不同 source text)。 三个 judge (GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash) 分别评测。每个 benchmark n=100。 与 LLMBar 结果交叉比较，形成 3×3 矩阵。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate\": 0.67,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_p\": 0.012,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate\": 0.61,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_p\": 0.048,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate\": 0.7,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_p\": 0.004,\n      \"alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass\": 0.9,\n      \"alpacaeval_nli_mean\": 0.908,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate\": 0.65,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_p\": 0.018,\n      \"mtbench_claude_formal_winrate\": 0.6,\n      \"mtbench_claude_p\": 0.065,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate\": 0.68,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_p\": 0.008,\n      \"mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass\": 0.87,\n      \"mtbench_nli_mean\": 0.882,\n      \"n_benchmarks_with_gap\": 3,\n      \"significant_combos_total\": 7,\n      \"total_combos\": 9,\n      \"non_significant_combos\": [\n        \"Claude×MT-Bench (p=0.065, borderline)\"\n      ],\n      \"borderline_combos\": 1,\n      \"mean_winrate_across_all_9\": 0.664\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"LLMBar\",\n          \"AlpacaEval\",\n          \"MT-Bench\",\n          \"Mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"69.1%**\",\n            \"67.0%*\",\n            \"65.0%*\",\n            \"67.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            \"64.0%*\",\n            \"61.0%*\",\n            \"60.0%†\",\n            \"61.7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            \"72.4%**\",\n            \"70.0%**\",\n            \"68.0%**\",\n            \"70.1%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            \"68.5%\",\n            \"66.0%\",\n            \"64.3%\",\n            \"66.3%\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"** p<0.01, * p<0.05, † p<0.10. n=100 per cell, n_consistent varies 48-58.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 4: Counterfactual Quality per Benchmark\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"n\",\n          \"NLI Pass Rate\",\n          \"NLI Mean\",\n          \"BERTScore Mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            100,\n            \"88%\",\n            0.896,\n            0.842\n          ],\n          [\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            100,\n            \"90%\",\n            0.908,\n            0.851\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            100,\n            \"87%\",\n            0.882,\n            0.835\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"A2 假设成立：3/3 benchmarks 显示 gap。Benchmark 梯度 (LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench) 有方法论意义——task-specific evaluation criteria 越强，style bias 越被抑制。 Judge 梯度 (Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定跨 benchmark，说明 judge 的 style sensitivity 是其内在属性而非 benchmark artifact。9 个组合的 mean win rate 0.664 在 cross_judge_formal_win_rate [0.60, 0.75] 范围内。\\n\\n\\nFormality bias 跨 benchmark 泛化，因为 bias 源于 judge 内在偏好而非特定数据集特征。 AlpacaEval 效应略强于 MT-Bench：open-ended instruction-following 任务给 style variation 更大空间，formal tone 作为 quality proxy 权重更大；MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构和更 specific 的评判标准 (如 math/reasoning accuracy) 部分抑制了 style 影响。Claude×MT-Bench 是唯一 borderline 不显著的组合 (p=0.065)，因为 Claude 在有明确正确性标准的 benchmark 上更倾向 content-based 判断，且 Claude 本身 formality sensitivity 最低。NLI pass rate 在 AlpacaEval (0.90) 略高于 MT-Bench (0.87)，因为 AlpacaEval response 结构更简单， counterfactual 改写更容易保持语义。7/9 显著远超偶然水平。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n    \"description\": \"对 exp-001/002 的每个 judge×benchmark 组合，计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统性比较两种 measurement 的 sensitivity。同一 counterfactual 数据。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llmbar_gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.1,\n      \"llmbar_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.332,\n      \"llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_p\": 0.006,\n      \"llmbar_claude_likert_ate\": 0.06,\n      \"llmbar_claude_likert_p\": 0.485,\n      \"llmbar_claude_pairwise_p\": 0.028,\n      \"llmbar_gemini_likert_ate\": 0.14,\n      \"llmbar_gemini_likert_p\": 0.198,\n      \"llmbar_gemini_pairwise_p\": 0.002,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.08,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.412,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_likert_ate\": 0.04,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_likert_p\": 0.551,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_likert_ate\": 0.12,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_likert_p\": 0.142,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.09,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.388,\n      \"mtbench_claude_likert_ate\": 0.03,\n      \"mtbench_claude_likert_p\": 0.612,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_likert_ate\": 0.11,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_likert_p\": 0.175,\n      \"combos_with_gap\": 7,\n      \"combos_without_gap\": 2,\n      \"combos_total\": 9,\n      \"gap_note\": \"2 个无 gap：Claude×MT-Bench (两者都不显著，一致性 non-sig)，Gemini×AlpacaEval Likert p=0.142 borderline\",\n      \"median_likert_p\": 0.388,\n      \"median_pairwise_p\": 0.012,\n      \"cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median\": 0.37,\n      \"no_reverse_pattern\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 5: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — The Likert Blindspot\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge × Benchmark\",\n          \"Likert ATE\",\n          \"Likert p\",\n          \"Pairwise WR\",\n          \"Pairwise p\",\n          \"Gap?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o × LLMBar\",\n            \"+0.10\",\n            \"0.332\",\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude × LLMBar\",\n            \"+0.06\",\n            \"0.485\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"0.028*\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini × LLMBar\",\n            \"+0.14\",\n            \"0.198\",\n            \"72.4%\",\n            \"0.002**\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\",\n            \"+0.08\",\n            \"0.412\",\n            \"67.0%\",\n            \"0.012*\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude × AlpacaEval\",\n            \"+0.04\",\n            \"0.551\",\n            \"61.0%\",\n            \"0.048*\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini × AlpacaEval\",\n            \"+0.12\",\n            \"0.142\",\n            \"70.0%\",\n            \"0.004**\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\",\n            \"+0.09\",\n            \"0.388\",\n            \"65.0%\",\n            \"0.018*\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude × MT-Bench\",\n            \"+0.03\",\n            \"0.612\",\n            \"60.0%\",\n            \"0.065†\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini × MT-Bench\",\n            \"+0.11\",\n            \"0.175\",\n            \"68.0%\",\n            \"0.008**\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"Gap = Likert p>0.10 AND Pairwise p<0.05. 7/9 combos show gap. 0/9 reverse pattern.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"C2 的核心 evidence。7/9 组合出现系统性 measurement gap，且无 reverse pattern (没有任何组合 Likert 显著但 Pairwise 不显著)。median Likert p = 0.37 在 [0.15, 0.5] 范围内， median Pairwise p = 0.012 在 [0.001, 0.02] 范围内。gap 不依赖特定 judge 或 benchmark—— 这意味着现有文献中基于 Likert 的 style bias 研究可能系统性低估问题严重程度。 Practical implication: style bias audit 应使用 pairwise comparison 而非 pointwise scoring。\\n\\n\\nLikert-Pairwise gap 的根因是 measurement scale 的信息结构差异。Likert pointwise 评分中， style bias 被三个机制稀释：(1) score anchoring——judge 倾向使用量表中段，微小 style 偏好 不足以跨越 score boundary；(2) absolute calibration noise——不同 item 的 baseline quality 差异远大于 style 引入的差异，between-item variance 淹没 within-item style effect； (3) 离散量表的 resolution limit——1-10 scale 上 0.10 的 ATE 被四舍五入吸收。 Pairwise 直接呈现 A/B 对比，消除 absolute calibration 问题，将 style 差异放大为 forced choice 中的 tie-breaking signal。Gemini 的 Likert p (0.142-0.198) 最接近显著， 因为 Gemini 的 formality premium 最强 (72.4%)，即使 Likert 的稀释也无法完全消除。 但仍未达 p<0.05，确认 Likert blindspot 的系统性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) — negative control\",\n    \"description\": \"D014 Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。Epistemic commitment change 与 NLI verification 结构性不兼容。本实验以 pilot 数据 (n=20) 为基础，正式文档化失败模式， 作为 C3 的 axis boundary evidence。不需额外 API 调用。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_pilot\": 20,\n      \"nli_cf_pass_rate\": 0.65,\n      \"nli_cf_mean\": 0.704,\n      \"bertscore_cf_mean\": 0.92,\n      \"joint_pass_rate\": 0.45,\n      \"by_tone_assertive_both_pass\": 0.385,\n      \"by_tone_hedging_both_pass\": 0.571,\n      \"catastrophic_nli_lt001_count\": 6,\n      \"catastrophic_fraction\": 0.3,\n      \"failure_mode\": \"assertive→hedging 改变 epistemic commitment (confidence markers, modal verbs)，NLI 正确检测为 non-entailment\",\n      \"structural_incompatibility\": true,\n      \"pipeline_stopped_at\": \"content_verification\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table A1: Tone Axis Content Verification Failure (n=20 pilot)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Direction\",\n          \"n\",\n          \"NLI Mean\",\n          \"Both Pass Rate\",\n          \"Catastrophic NLI<0.01\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Assertive→Hedging\",\n            13,\n            \"0.656\",\n            \"38.5%\",\n            \"4/13 (30.8%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Hedging→Assertive\",\n            7,\n            \"0.793\",\n            \"57.1%\",\n            \"2/7 (28.6%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Overall\",\n            20,\n            \"0.704\",\n            \"45.0%\",\n            \"6/20 (30.0%)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Tone 作为 negative control 为 C3 提供 principled method boundary：CSD 适用于 不改变认知承诺的 surface-level style axes (formality ✓)，不适用于改变 epistemic commitment 的 axes (tone ✗)。NLI gate 在此处正确拒绝—— 这不是方法失败，而是正确的质量控制行为。Paper 中定位为 \\\"method boundary\\\" 而非 \\\"negative result\\\"，因为它回答了 \\\"CSD 适用范围\\\" 这个审稿人一定会问的问题。\\n\\n\\nTone 改变 (assertive↔hedging) 不是纯 style 变换——它改变了说话者对命题的认知承诺程度。 \\\"X is the best approach\\\" vs \\\"X might be a reasonable approach\\\" 在 NLI 框架下不构成双向蕴含， 因为前者的 truth conditions 严格强于后者。30% 的样本出现 catastrophic NLI<0.01， 说明这不是 threshold 选择问题而是根本性的语义兼容性问题。Hedging 方向 (assertive→hedging) both_pass 更高 (57.1% vs 38.5%)，因为弱化断言仍蕴含弱化后的命题，但强化断言 (hedging→assertive) 引入了原文未承诺的确定性。这个不对称性本身就是 principled boundary 的证据：NLI gate 不是 arbitrary obstacle，而是正确识别了语义改变。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n    \"description\": \"Original text vs 同风格 double-rewrite 的 pairwise 比较，量化 original preference confound。 D015: 扩展到所有 judge × LLMBar 组合。同时分析 casual-original subset (main pairwise 中原文为 casual 的子集) 在不同 judge 上的 formal win rate。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_n_valid\": 95,\n      \"gpt4o_n_consistent\": 60,\n      \"gpt4o_original_wins\": 32,\n      \"gpt4o_rewrite_wins\": 28,\n      \"gpt4o_original_win_rate\": 0.533,\n      \"gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.362,\n      \"gpt4o_wilson_ci\": [\n        0.408,\n        0.655\n      ],\n      \"claude_n_consistent\": 55,\n      \"claude_original_wins\": 28,\n      \"claude_rewrite_wins\": 27,\n      \"claude_original_win_rate\": 0.509,\n      \"claude_sign_test_p\": 0.92,\n      \"gemini_n_consistent\": 62,\n      \"gemini_original_wins\": 34,\n      \"gemini_rewrite_wins\": 28,\n      \"gemini_original_win_rate\": 0.548,\n      \"gemini_sign_test_p\": 0.28,\n      \"mean_original_win_rate\": 0.53,\n      \"any_judge_original_pref_significant\": false,\n      \"casual_orig_gpt4o_formal_wr\": 0.545,\n      \"casual_orig_gpt4o_p\": 0.832,\n      \"casual_orig_gpt4o_n\": 22,\n      \"casual_orig_claude_formal_wr\": 0.63,\n      \"casual_orig_claude_p\": 0.072,\n      \"casual_orig_claude_n\": 27,\n      \"casual_orig_gemini_formal_wr\": 0.611,\n      \"casual_orig_gemini_p\": 0.096,\n      \"casual_orig_gemini_n\": 36,\n      \"casual_orig_best_judge\": \"Claude\",\n      \"casual_orig_best_judge_wr\": 0.63,\n      \"casual_orig_best_judge_p\": 0.072\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 6: Original Preference Control Across Judges (LLMBar)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Original Wins\",\n          \"Rewrite Wins\",\n          \"Original WR\",\n          \"p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            60,\n            32,\n            28,\n            \"53.3%\",\n            \"0.362\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            55,\n            28,\n            27,\n            \"50.9%\",\n            \"0.920\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            62,\n            34,\n            28,\n            \"54.8%\",\n            \"0.280\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 7: Casual-Original Subset — Formal Win Rate When Opposing Original Preference\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Formal Wins\",\n          \"Formal WR\",\n          \"p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            22,\n            12,\n            \"54.5%\",\n            \"0.832\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            27,\n            17,\n            \"63.0%\",\n            \"0.072†\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            36,\n            22,\n            \"61.1%\",\n            \"0.096†\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"† p<0.10. Formal = rewrite in this subset, so original preference opposes formality.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"A6 假设成立：original preference 贡献 <5 个百分点 (mean 53% - 50% = 3%)， 远小于 formality premium (mean 68.5% - 50% = 18.5%)。Casual-original subset 在 Claude (63%) 和 Gemini (61.1%) 上均 >60%，best judge p=0.072 满足 p<0.10。 casual_orig_best_judge_wr 0.63 在 [0.60, 0.70] 范围内。 Direction asymmetry (MVP 中 formal-orig 78.8% vs casual-orig 54.5%) 主要解释 从 \\\"original preference\\\" 转向 \\\"改写方向的非对称难度\\\"。\\n\\n\\nOriginal preference 在所有 judge 上均弱且不显著 (mean 53.0%)，因为 double-rewrite 过程 虽引入轻微 rewrite artifact (如稍微不自然的措辞)，但这个 artifact 对 judge 影响是随机的 而非系统性的。Claude 的 original preference 最弱 (50.9%)，可能因为 Claude 对 \\\"naturalness\\\" 的敏感度更低。Gemini 稍高 (54.8%)，可能因为轻量模型对 fluency 微妙差异更敏感。 Casual-original subset 分析是关键：Claude 上 63.0% formal win rate (p=0.072) 说明即使 formality preference 与 original preference 方向相反 (formal = rewrite)， formality 仍占上风。这在 GPT-4o 上不显著 (54.5%) 可能因为 GPT-4o 的 original preference (53.3%) 与 formality preference 恰好在 casual-original subset 上互相抵消。 Claude original preference 更弱 (50.9%)，所以 formality 更容易 dominate。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=500)\",\n    \"description\": \"将 formality pairwise 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。选择效应最强的 judge×benchmark 组合 (Gemini×LLMBar)。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。 五个 n=100 子组的稳定性分析。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_total\": 500,\n      \"n_valid_both_trials\": 490,\n      \"n_consistent\": 278,\n      \"consistency_rate\": 0.567,\n      \"formal_wins\": 184,\n      \"casual_wins\": 94,\n      \"formal_win_rate\": 0.662,\n      \"wilson_ci\": [\n        0.604,\n        0.716\n      ],\n      \"sign_test_p\": 1e-05,\n      \"cohens_h\": 0.337,\n      \"likert_ate_n500\": 0.11,\n      \"likert_ate_p_n500\": 0.082,\n      \"likert_still_borderline\": true,\n      \"sub1_winrate\": 0.7,\n      \"sub2_winrate\": 0.65,\n      \"sub3_winrate\": 0.68,\n      \"sub4_winrate\": 0.64,\n      \"sub5_winrate\": 0.64,\n      \"subgroup_sd\": 0.026,\n      \"power_n100_d065\": 0.72,\n      \"power_n300_d065\": 0.97,\n      \"power_n500_d065\": 0.995,\n      \"min_detectable_wr_n500\": 0.56,\n      \"nli_ge90_n_consistent\": 232,\n      \"nli_ge90_winrate\": 0.685,\n      \"nli_ge80_n_consistent\": 262,\n      \"nli_ge80_winrate\": 0.668\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 8: Scaled Replication (Gemini × LLMBar, Formality)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scale\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Formal WR\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Pairwise p\",\n          \"Likert p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"n=100 (MVP pilot)\",\n            55,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            \"0.332\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n=500 (replication)\",\n            278,\n            \"66.2%\",\n            \"[60.4%, 71.6%]\",\n            \"<0.001***\",\n            \"0.082†\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"Likert p still non-significant at n=500 (borderline), confirming structural measurement gap.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 9: Subgroup Stability (5 × n=100 splits)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Split\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Formal WR\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Block 1\",\n            57,\n            \"70.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Block 2\",\n            53,\n            \"65.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Block 3\",\n            56,\n            \"68.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Block 4\",\n            54,\n            \"64.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Block 5\",\n            58,\n            \"64.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full n=500\",\n            278,\n            \"66.2%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 10: Power Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n\",\n          \"Power (WR=0.65)\",\n          \"Min Detectable WR (power=0.80)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            100,\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"62.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            300,\n            \"0.97\",\n            \"57.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            500,\n            \"0.995\",\n            \"56.0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"n500_formal_win_rate 0.662 在 [0.58, 0.70] 范围内。p<0.001 满足 p<0.01 核心假设。 n=500 Likert 仍 borderline (p=0.082) 是 C2 的额外弹药——即使 5× sample size 都不能 让 Likert 检测到 pairwise 在 n=100 就发现的效应。Power analysis 解释了 why： pairwise within-subject design 的 effective sample size 远大于 Likert between-subject。\\n\\n\\nn=500 时 win rate 0.662 相比 n=100 pilot 的 0.691 有 2.9% 的 regression to mean， 这在预期范围内——pilot 的 point estimate 在 CI [0.56, 0.80] 上端，larger sample 收敛到 true effect。CI 从 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.60, 0.72]，p 从 0.006 降到 <0.001。 五个 n=100 子组 win rate 在 0.64-0.70 范围波动 (σ=0.026)，展示效应高度稳定。 关键发现：即使 n=500，Likert ATE 仍仅 borderline 显著 (p=0.082)——这强化了 C2： Likert blindspot 不是 power 问题，而是 measurement sensitivity 的结构性差异。 如果仅仅是 power 问题，n=500 的 Likert 应当显著；它仍不显著说明 Likert 对 style bias 的检测本身就是 structurally impaired。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\",\n    \"description\": \"第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变词汇和句法 但不改变信息内容。Full pipeline: counterfactual gen → NLI verification → dual-direction pairwise scoring。三个 judge × LLMBar，n=100。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"register_nli_pass_rate\": 0.86,\n      \"register_nli_mean\": 0.893,\n      \"register_bertscore_mean\": 0.839,\n      \"register_both_pass\": 0.83,\n      \"gpt4o_academic_win_rate\": 0.66,\n      \"gpt4o_n_consistent\": 53,\n      \"gpt4o_p\": 0.015,\n      \"claude_academic_win_rate\": 0.62,\n      \"claude_n_consistent\": 50,\n      \"claude_p\": 0.042,\n      \"gemini_academic_win_rate\": 0.714,\n      \"gemini_n_consistent\": 56,\n      \"gemini_p\": 0.003,\n      \"judges_significant\": 3,\n      \"mean_academic_winrate\": 0.665,\n      \"gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.289,\n      \"claude_likert_p\": 0.511,\n      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.167,\n      \"register_likert_pairwise_gap\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table A2: Register (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Academic Wins\",\n          \"Conv. Wins\",\n          \"Win Rate\",\n          \"Pairwise p\",\n          \"Likert p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            53,\n            35,\n            18,\n            \"66.0%\",\n            \"0.015*\",\n            \"0.289\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            50,\n            31,\n            19,\n            \"62.0%\",\n            \"0.042*\",\n            \"0.511\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            56,\n            40,\n            16,\n            \"71.4%\",\n            \"0.003**\",\n            \"0.167\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table A3: Cross-Axis Summary (LLMBar, 3 judges)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Axis\",\n          \"Mean WR\",\n          \"Judges Sig. (3)\",\n          \"NLI Pass\",\n          \"Likert Detects?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Formality\",\n            \"68.5%\",\n            \"3/3\",\n            \"88%\",\n            \"0/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Register\",\n            \"66.5%\",\n            \"3/3\",\n            \"86%\",\n            \"0/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Tone\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"65% (failed)\",\n            \"N/A\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Verbosity\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"65% (failed)\",\n            \"N/A\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Register 作为第二个 working axis 将 C3 从 \\\"only formality works\\\" 提升为 \\\"content-preserving surface-level axes generally work\\\"。效应量级系统性排序 formality > register > (tone/verbosity failed)，与 linguistic level 数量正相关： formality 跨词汇+句法+语用，register 跨词汇+句法，tone 主要在语用层。 这提供了 principled taxonomy：改变 surface form 而不改变 information content 或 epistemic commitment 的 axes 适用于 CSD。\\n\\n\\nRegister (academic vs conversational) 是 surface-level 词汇+句法变换，不改变信息内容： Latinate 术语 vs everyday words, 复杂从句 vs 简单句, disciplinary jargon vs lay terms。 效应在 formality 和 tone 之间 (mean 0.665)，因为 register 涉及词汇和句法层面变化 但比 formality 更窄——formality 包含 register + tone + 其他 cues 的 composite。 NLI pass 0.86 略低于 formality (0.88)，因为 academic vocabulary 有时引入微妙语义偏移 (术语替代 layman terms 可能 shift specificity)。Judge 梯度保持 Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude， 进一步确认这是 judge 内在属性而非 axis-specific 现象。所有 Likert p 均不显著， 扩展了 C2 blindspot evidence 到第二个 axis。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为替代 rewriter，对 LLMBar formality 运行完整 pipeline。 与 Qwen3-32B 结果比较，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。GPT-4o 作为 judge。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n      \"llama_nli_mean\": 0.881,\n      \"llama_bertscore_mean\": 0.836,\n      \"llama_n_consistent\": 52,\n      \"llama_formal_win_rate\": 0.66,\n      \"llama_sign_test_p\": 0.015,\n      \"qwen_nli_pass_rate\": 0.88,\n      \"qwen_formal_win_rate\": 0.691,\n      \"qwen_sign_test_p\": 0.006,\n      \"winrate_difference\": 0.031,\n      \"fisher_exact_p_for_difference\": 0.42,\n      \"rewriter_effect_significant\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table A4: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Rewriter\",\n          \"NLI Pass\",\n          \"Formal WR\",\n          \"Pairwise p\",\n          \"n_consistent\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"88%\",\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            55\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-70B\",\n            \"85%\",\n            \"66.0%\",\n            \"0.015*\",\n            52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Difference\",\n            \"-3%\",\n            \"-3.1%\",\n            \"Fisher p=0.42\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix 级实验，但对 reviewer 质疑 rewriter choice 时提供决定性回应。 两个不同 family 的 rewriter 产生一致的 formality premium，确认效应的 robustness。\\n\\n\\nLlama rewriter 产生略低但仍显著的 formality premium (0.66 vs 0.69)，差异不显著 (Fisher p=0.42)。NLI pass rate 略低 (0.85 vs 0.88) 因为 Llama-70B 在 instruction following 上略弱于 Qwen3-32B (后者受益于 Qwen3 的强 instruction tuning)，导致少量 counterfactual 有轻微语义偏移。3% win rate 差异在统计噪声范围内，排除了 \\\"Qwen rewriter 引入某种被 judge 偏好的 writing pattern\\\" 的 confound。 关键论点：formality bias 检测不依赖于特定 rewriter family。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\",\n    \"description\": \"DREAM CRITICAL。对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 sign test：每对中 formal version 的 Likert score 是否严格高于 casual version？如果 binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 是 test choice 差异，非 measurement method 差异。如果不显著 → 确认 C2。 零成本重分析。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"data_source\": \"scored_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar, n=88 primary)\",\n      \"n_primary\": 88,\n      \"n_formal_higher\": 29,\n      \"n_casual_higher\": 21,\n      \"n_tied\": 38,\n      \"tie_fraction\": 0.432,\n      \"n_non_tied\": 50,\n      \"binarized_formal_rate\": 0.58,\n      \"sign_test_p\": 0.24,\n      \"is_significant\": false,\n      \"strict_binarize_diff_ge2\": {\n        \"n_non_tied\": 18,\n        \"formal_wins\": 11,\n        \"sign_test_p\": 0.48\n      },\n      \"pairwise_formal_wr\": 0.691,\n      \"pairwise_p\": 0.006,\n      \"gap_confirmed\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 11: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise — C2 Decisive Test\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"n (non-tied/consistent)\",\n          \"Formal Rate\",\n          \"Sign Test p\",\n          \"Conclusion\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pairwise (position-controlled)\",\n            55,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            \"Significant bias detected\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binarized Likert (score > comparison)\",\n            50,\n            \"58.0%\",\n            \"0.240\",\n            \"Not significant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binarized Likert (diff ≥ 2)\",\n            18,\n            \"61.1%\",\n            \"0.481\",\n            \"Not significant\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"Same underlying data (scored_32b.jsonl). Pairwise detects what binarized Likert misses.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"THIS IS THE DECISIVE EVIDENCE FOR C2。binarized_likert_sign_p = 0.24 在 [0.12, 1.0] 范围内。 排除了 \\\"Likert 和 Pairwise 用不同 statistical test 所以不可比\\\" 的 alternative explanation。 现在三种分析都使用 sign test on binary outcome，唯一差异是 measurement method： (1) Pairwise forced-choice → 69.1%, p=0.006 (2) Binarized Likert score comparison → 58.0%, p=0.24 (3) Raw Likert ATE → p=0.33 Pairwise 胜出是因为它消除了 Likert 的 tie problem (43% tied) 和 between-item calibration noise。 Main Result Table 中增加 Binarized Likert 列是 C2 的命门证据。\\n\\n\\nBinarized Likert 不显著 (p=0.24) 的根因是 Likert scale 的 discretization loss。 在 1-10 量表上，formality 引入的 quality perception 差异约 0.10 分 (从 Likert ATE)， 这远小于一个 scale step。因此 43.2% 的 pair 获得相同 Likert score (tied)——这些 pair 中 judge 确实感知到了 formality 差异 (pairwise 中会做出选择)，但 Likert 的 粗粒度量表无法捕捉这个差异。在 50 个 non-tied pairs 中，formal 略占优 (58%) 但 sample size 太小 (n=50 而非 pairwise 的 n=55 consistent)，sign test power 不足。 即使用更严格的 binarization (score difference ≥ 2)，n 降到 18，formal 11/18 (61%) 但 p=0.48 更加不显著。关键 insight: pairwise 的 forced-choice 消除了 tie 问题—— judge 必须在两个版本间选择，将 Likert 中被 tie 掩盖的微弱偏好显现出来。 这证明 Likert-Pairwise gap 是 measurement granularity 差异，非 statistical test 选择差异。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"在 70%, 75%, 80%, 85%, 90%, 95% 六个 NLI threshold 上重新计算 formality pairwise results。 验证结论对 threshold 选择的 robustness。零成本重分析已有 pairwise_32b 数据。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"data_source\": \"pairwise_results_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\",\n      \"thresholds\": {\n        \"nli_70\": {\n          \"n_pairs_pass\": 96,\n          \"n_consistent\": 53,\n          \"formal_wins\": 37,\n          \"formal_wr\": 0.698,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.005\n        },\n        \"nli_75\": {\n          \"n_pairs_pass\": 94,\n          \"n_consistent\": 52,\n          \"formal_wins\": 36,\n          \"formal_wr\": 0.692,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.006\n        },\n        \"nli_80\": {\n          \"n_pairs_pass\": 88,\n          \"n_consistent\": 50,\n          \"formal_wins\": 35,\n          \"formal_wr\": 0.7,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.005\n        },\n        \"nli_85\": {\n          \"n_pairs_pass\": 72,\n          \"n_consistent\": 42,\n          \"formal_wins\": 31,\n          \"formal_wr\": 0.738,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.003\n        },\n        \"nli_90\": {\n          \"n_pairs_pass\": 52,\n          \"n_consistent\": 46,\n          \"formal_wins\": 34,\n          \"formal_wr\": 0.739,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.002\n        },\n        \"nli_95\": {\n          \"n_pairs_pass\": 36,\n          \"n_consistent\": 28,\n          \"formal_wins\": 21,\n          \"formal_wr\": 0.75,\n          \"sign_test_p\": 0.013\n        }\n      },\n      \"all_significant_70_to_95\": true,\n      \"winrate_trend\": \"monotonically increasing (0.698 → 0.750)\",\n      \"p_value_trend\": \"decreasing then increasing (0.005 → 0.002 → 0.013) due to n tradeoff\",\n      \"significant_range\": \"70%-95%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 12: NLI Threshold Sensitivity (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality Pairwise)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"NLI Threshold\",\n          \"n_pass\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Formal WR\",\n          \"Sign Test p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"≥70%\",\n            96,\n            53,\n            \"69.8%\",\n            \"0.005**\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"≥75%\",\n            94,\n            52,\n            \"69.2%\",\n            \"0.006**\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"≥80%\",\n            88,\n            50,\n            \"70.0%\",\n            \"0.005**\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"≥85%\",\n            72,\n            42,\n            \"73.8%\",\n            \"0.003**\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"≥90%\",\n            52,\n            46,\n            \"73.9%\",\n            \"0.002**\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"≥95%\",\n            36,\n            28,\n            \"75.0%\",\n            \"0.013*\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"All thresholds from 70% to 95% yield significant results. Default threshold: 80%.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"nli_threshold_sensitivity_significant_range = ['70%-95%']，完美匹配核心假设。 结论不依赖 threshold 选择——从最宽松 (70%) 到最严格 (95%) 均显著。 Win rate 随 threshold 上升这一 monotonic trend 说明 content preservation quality 与 formality effect purity 正相关，支持 CSD 的 causal interpretation。\\n\\n\\nFormality effect 在所有 NLI threshold 上均显著，因为 formality 改写是高质量的 surface-level 变换——即使在宽松 threshold (70%) 下加入的额外 pairs 中有一些 semantic drift， formality premium 仍然 dominant。Win rate 随 threshold 提高而单调递增 (0.698→0.750)， 说明 cleaner pairs (higher NLI) 的 formality effect 更纯——content preservation 越好， observed bias 越接近 true causal effect。p 值在 85-90% 处最低 (0.002)，因为此处 n (42-46) 与 effect size (0.74) 达到最佳平衡；95% threshold 下 n 降到 28， 尽管 effect size 最高 (0.75)，power 损失导致 p 略升至 0.013，但仍远低于 0.05。 Tone 的 NLI 在 72% 处 borderline——sensitivity analysis 显示即使在 70% threshold 下 formality 仍稳健，这不是 threshold tuning 的结果。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Consistency filter bias analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"比较 position-consistent pairs vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text lengths、 task types，检查 42-52% 的 discard rate 是否引入系统性偏差。零成本重分析。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"data_source\": \"pairwise_results_32b.jsonl\",\n      \"total_valid_pairs\": 98,\n      \"n_consistent\": 55,\n      \"n_inconsistent\": 43,\n      \"discard_rate\": 0.439,\n      \"consistent_nli_mean\": 0.903,\n      \"inconsistent_nli_mean\": 0.886,\n      \"nli_ttest_p\": 0.42,\n      \"nli_difference_significant\": false,\n      \"consistent_text_length_mean\": 142.3,\n      \"inconsistent_text_length_mean\": 137.8,\n      \"length_ttest_p\": 0.58,\n      \"length_difference_significant\": false,\n      \"consistent_formal_orig_fraction\": 0.6,\n      \"inconsistent_formal_orig_fraction\": 0.558,\n      \"orig_style_chi2_p\": 0.67,\n      \"orig_style_difference_significant\": false,\n      \"consistent_bertscore_mean\": 0.848,\n      \"inconsistent_bertscore_mean\": 0.834,\n      \"bertscore_ttest_p\": 0.38,\n      \"bertscore_difference_significant\": false,\n      \"task_type_chi2_p\": 0.73,\n      \"task_type_difference_significant\": false,\n      \"any_significant_difference\": false,\n      \"filter_introduces_bias\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table A5: Consistency Filter Bias Analysis (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Property\",\n          \"Consistent (n=55)\",\n          \"Inconsistent (n=43)\",\n          \"Test\",\n          \"p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"NLI Mean\",\n            \"0.903\",\n            \"0.886\",\n            \"t-test\",\n            \"0.42\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Text Length (words)\",\n            \"142.3\",\n            \"137.8\",\n            \"t-test\",\n            \"0.58\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BERTScore Mean\",\n            \"0.848\",\n            \"0.834\",\n            \"t-test\",\n            \"0.38\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Formal-Original %\",\n            \"60.0%\",\n            \"55.8%\",\n            \"χ²\",\n            \"0.67\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Task Type Distribution\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"χ²\",\n            \"0.73\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"No significant differences. Consistency filtering does not systematically bias the retained sample.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"所有 5 个 comparison 均不显著 (最小 p=0.38)，conclusively 排除 systematic filter bias。 42-52% 的 discard rate 虽高，但 discarded pairs 与 retained pairs 在 observables 上 indistinguishable。Reviewer 对 \\\"high discard rate → biased sample\\\" 的 concern 可用此表直接回应。建议放在 Appendix 作为 methodological robustness check。\\n\\n\\nPosition-consistency filtering 不引入系统性偏差，因为 position inconsistency 的主要来源 是 judge 的 confidence 而非 pair 的 systematic properties。Judge 对某些 pairs 有明确偏好 (无论位置如何都选同一个) → consistent，对另一些 pairs 犹豫不决 (位置影响选择) → inconsistent。 犹豫不决与 pair 的 NLI、text length、task type 无关，而与 quality 差异的微妙程度有关—— 当两个版本在 judge 眼中 \\\"差不多好\\\" 时，position 成为 tie-breaker。这是随机噪声， 不是对特定类型 pair 的系统性过滤。NLI 略高 (0.903 vs 0.886) 但 p=0.42 不显著， 说明 content preservation 质量不驱动 consistency。consistent pairs 中 formal-original fraction (0.60) 略高于 inconsistent (0.56)，但差异远不显著 (p=0.67)，排除了 \\\"filtering selects for original-preference-aligned pairs\\\" 的 confound。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Human NLI validation (80 annotations)\",\n    \"description\": \"Human validation of NLI gate decisions。对 80 个 counterfactual pairs 做人工标注： content 是否 preserved。报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen's κ)。 可使用 LLM-as-annotator (GPT-4) + human spot check 的混合策略。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_annotated\": 80,\n      \"n_nli_high\": 50,\n      \"n_nli_low\": 30,\n      \"human_preserved\": 62,\n      \"human_not_preserved\": 18,\n      \"human_preservation_rate\": 0.775,\n      \"nli_preserved\": 58,\n      \"nli_not_preserved\": 22,\n      \"both_preserved\": 54,\n      \"both_not_preserved\": 14,\n      \"nli_preserved_human_not\": 4,\n      \"nli_not_preserved_human_yes\": 8,\n      \"raw_agreement\": 0.85,\n      \"cohens_kappa\": 0.72,\n      \"kappa_interpretation\": \"substantial agreement\",\n      \"nli_false_positive_rate\": 0.069,\n      \"nli_false_negative_rate\": 0.129,\n      \"false_positive_pattern\": \"subtle information additions in formal rewrites that NLI misses\",\n      \"false_negative_pattern\": \"stylistic paraphrases that NLI over-penalizes as semantic change\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table A6: Human-NLI Agreement on Content Preservation (n=80)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"\",\n          \"Human: Preserved\",\n          \"Human: Not Preserved\",\n          \"Total\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"NLI: Preserved (≥0.80)\",\n            54,\n            4,\n            58\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NLI: Not Preserved (<0.80)\",\n            8,\n            14,\n            22\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Total\",\n            62,\n            18,\n            80\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"Cohen's κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement). NLI FPR = 6.9%, FNR = 12.9%.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"κ = 0.72 在 [0.61, 0.80] \\\"substantial\\\" 范围内，满足审稿人对 NLI gate 可信度的要求。 NLI 偏保守 (FNR > FPR) 对 CSD 有利：retained pairs 的 content preservation 质量 被 underestimate 而非 overestimate。建议论文中强调：\\\"NLI false positives are rare (6.9%), meaning pairs that pass the gate genuinely preserve content.\\\"\\n\\n\\nCohen's κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement) 因为 NLI 模型 (DeBERTa-large-MNLI) 的 training data 与 content preservation 判断高度对齐——NLI 本质上就是判断两个文本是否表达相同信息， 这与 \\\"counterfactual 是否保持 content\\\" 的判断完全一致。False positive rate 低 (6.9%) 说明 NLI gate 通过的 pairs 绝大多数确实 content-preserved——这是 CSD 结论可信度的基础。 False negative rate 较高 (12.9%) 说明 NLI 偏保守 (over-reject)，但这对 CSD 是安全的方向： over-rejection 意味着 retained pairs 的 content preservation 质量比 NLI score 建议的更高。 8 个 false negative 主要是 stylistic paraphrasing (如换用近义词或调整句子结构) 被 NLI 判为 non-entailment，但人工判断这些改变不影响信息内容。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\",\n    \"description\": \"Logistic regression 正式分离 formality 和 original preference。 Pool exp-001/002 所有 judge×benchmark pairwise 数据。DV: formal_preferred (1/0)。 IV: is_formal_original (1/0), judge (fixed effects), benchmark (fixed effects)。 Test formality 主效应 (intercept) 是否显著，interaction 是否不显著。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"data_source\": \"pooled pairwise from all judge × benchmark combinations\",\n      \"n_observations\": 459,\n      \"intercept_beta\": 0.52,\n      \"intercept_se\": 0.19,\n      \"intercept_z\": 2.74,\n      \"intercept_p\": 0.006,\n      \"intercept_odds_ratio\": 1.68,\n      \"intercept_interpretation\": \"formal 被偏好的 odds 是 casual 的 1.68 倍，controlling for original status\",\n      \"is_formal_original_beta\": 0.34,\n      \"is_formal_original_se\": 0.17,\n      \"is_formal_original_z\": 2.0,\n      \"is_formal_original_p\": 0.046,\n      \"is_formal_original_or\": 1.4,\n      \"interaction_beta\": 0.12,\n      \"interaction_se\": 0.22,\n      \"interaction_z\": 0.55,\n      \"interaction_p\": 0.58,\n      \"interaction_significant\": false,\n      \"judge_claude_beta\": -0.28,\n      \"judge_claude_p\": 0.11,\n      \"judge_gemini_beta\": 0.19,\n      \"judge_gemini_p\": 0.24,\n      \"benchmark_alpacaeval_beta\": -0.08,\n      \"benchmark_alpacaeval_p\": 0.62,\n      \"benchmark_mtbench_beta\": -0.15,\n      \"benchmark_mtbench_p\": 0.38,\n      \"mcfadden_r2\": 0.042,\n      \"aic\": 582.3,\n      \"bic\": 611.7,\n      \"raw_mean_formal_wr\": 0.664,\n      \"original_preference_contribution\": 0.033,\n      \"csd_adjusted_formal_wr\": 0.631,\n      \"logistic_formality_coef_p\": 0.006\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 13: Logistic Regression — Formality vs Original Preference Decomposition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Predictor\",\n          \"β\",\n          \"SE\",\n          \"z\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"Odds Ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Intercept (formality effect)\",\n            \"0.52\",\n            \"0.19\",\n            \"2.74\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            \"1.68\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"is_formal_original\",\n            \"0.34\",\n            \"0.17\",\n            \"2.00\",\n            \"0.046*\",\n            \"1.40\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Interaction\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"0.583\",\n            \"1.13\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Judge: Claude (vs GPT-4o)\",\n            \"-0.28\",\n            \"0.17\",\n            \"-1.65\",\n            \"0.110\",\n            \"0.76\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Judge: Gemini (vs GPT-4o)\",\n            \"0.19\",\n            \"0.16\",\n            \"1.19\",\n            \"0.240\",\n            \"1.21\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Bench: AlpacaEval (vs LLMBar)\",\n            \"-0.08\",\n            \"0.16\",\n            \"-0.50\",\n            \"0.620\",\n            \"0.92\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Bench: MT-Bench (vs LLMBar)\",\n            \"-0.15\",\n            \"0.17\",\n            \"-0.88\",\n            \"0.380\",\n            \"0.86\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"N=459 observations pooled across 9 judge×benchmark combinations. McFadden R²=0.042.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 14: CSD-Adjusted Win Rate\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\",\n          \"Source\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Raw formal win rate (mean across combos)\",\n            \"66.4%\",\n            \"exp-001/002\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Original preference contribution\",\n            \"+3.3%\",\n            \"exp-014 β₁\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CSD-adjusted formal win rate\",\n            \"63.1%\",\n            \"Raw − original contribution\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"95% CI of adjusted rate\",\n            \"[57.2%, 69.0%]\",\n            \"Bootstrap\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"logistic_formality_coef_p = 0.006 在 [0.001, 0.05] 范围内。Interaction p = 0.58 明确不显著。C4 (practical guidance) 有了统计基础：CSD-adjusted win rate 公式为 adjusted_wr = raw_wr - β₁/(β₀+β₁) × (raw_wr - 0.50)。这比 ad-hoc additive correction 更有统计根据。Paper 可以给出 practitioner checklist：(1) use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit; (2) run RATE control to quantify original preference; (3) report both raw and CSD-adjusted win rates; (4) verify content preservation per axis before applying CSD。\\n\\nFormality 主效应 (intercept β₀=0.52, p=0.006) 显著，说明控制 original status 后 formal 仍被系统性偏好——这是 formality bias 作为 independent causal effect 的统计证据。 is_formal_original (β₁=0.34, p=0.046) 边缘显著，说明 original preference 确实存在 但效应量 (OR=1.40) 远小于 formality (OR=1.68)。关键：interaction term 不显著 (p=0.58)， 意味着 formality 的效应不依赖于 formal 版本是否为 original——无论 formal 是原文还是改写， judge 都偏好它。这彻底回应了 \\\"observed formality bias 只是 original preference 的 proxy\\\" 的 alternative explanation。Judge 和 benchmark fixed effects 不显著，说明 formality premium 在不同 judge 和 benchmark 间是 stable 的 (尽管 magnitude 有差异， 但 direction 一致)。CSD-adjusted formal win rate = 63.1% (扣除 original preference 贡献 3.3 个百分点)，这是对 reviewer 最保守友好的 headline number。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1250,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1250}}}
